// Auto-generated for the Unit Board — 學測/IELTS/TOEFL Topic 5
window.I5_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"Stress & the Body 壓力與身體反應","cards":[{"w":"pressure","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of worry caused by too much to do","c":"壓力","s":"Many senior high students feel a lot of pressure before the entrance exam, so teachers try to keep the classroom calm and friendly.","t":"許多高三學生在升學考試前感受到很大的壓力,所以老師們試著讓教室保持平靜和友善。"},{"w":"strain","p":"n.","d":"a difficult situation that makes you tired or worried","c":"負擔;壓力","s":"Looking after her sick father and working full-time put a huge strain on Amy, and she started to lose sleep.","t":"照顧生病的父親又要全職工作,給艾咪帶來了巨大的負擔,她開始失眠。"},{"w":"adrenaline","p":"n.","d":"a body chemical that gives energy when you are scared or excited","c":"腎上腺素","s":"When the fire alarm suddenly rang, a rush of adrenaline made my heart race, and I ran down the stairs very quickly.","t":"火災警報突然響起時,一股腎上腺素讓我心跳加速,我很快地跑下樓梯。"},{"w":"heartbeat","p":"n.","d":"the sound or movement of your heart","c":"心跳","s":"I could hear my own heartbeat in my ears as I walked onto the stage, but I took a slow breath and began my speech.","t":"走上舞台時,我在耳朵裡能聽見自己的心跳,但我慢慢吸了一口氣,然後開始演講。"},{"w":"pulse","p":"n.","d":"how fast your heart is beating, felt at the wrist","c":"脈搏","s":"The nurse checked my pulse after the long run, and she said it was still high because my body was under stress.","t":"長跑之後護士檢查了我的脈搏,她說脈搏還是很快,因為我的身體正處於壓力之下。"},{"w":"sweat","p":"v.","d":"to have water come out of your skin","c":"流汗","s":"Ben always starts to sweat when he has to speak English in front of the class, so he keeps a small towel in his bag.","t":"班每次要在全班面前說英文時就開始流汗,所以他在書包裡放了一條小毛巾。"},{"w":"tremble","p":"v.","d":"to shake slightly because you are afraid or nervous","c":"顫抖","s":"My hands began to tremble when I opened the envelope with my test results, but I was relieved to see a good score.","t":"我打開裝著考試成績的信封時,雙手開始顫抖,但看到好成績我就鬆了一口氣。"},{"w":"panic","p":"v.","d":"to suddenly feel so afraid that you cannot think clearly","c":"驚慌","s":"Don't panic if you cannot answer the first question, because you can skip it and come back to it later.","t":"如果第一題答不出來,不要驚慌,因為你可以先跳過,之後再回來作答。"},{"w":"nervous","p":"adj.","d":"worried and a little afraid about something","c":"緊張的","s":"Lisa felt very nervous before her job interview, so she practised her answers with her sister the night before.","t":"麗莎在工作面試前感到非常緊張,所以她前一天晚上和姊姊一起練習回答問題。"},{"w":"tense","p":"adj.","d":"unable to relax because you are worried","c":"緊繃的","s":"The atmosphere in the office was tense before the big meeting, and nobody wanted to tell jokes or chat.","t":"大會議開始前,辦公室裡的氣氛很緊繃,沒有人想說笑或閒聊。"},{"w":"headache","p":"n.","d":"a pain in your head","c":"頭痛","s":"I often get a bad headache when I stay up late studying, so I now try to go to bed before midnight.","t":"我熬夜讀書時常常會頭痛,所以現在我試著在午夜前上床睡覺。"},{"w":"exhaustion","p":"n.","d":"the state of being extremely tired","c":"筋疲力盡","s":"After three nights of little sleep, Tom was suffering from exhaustion, and his doctor told him to rest for a few days.","t":"連續三晚睡得很少之後,湯姆陷入筋疲力盡的狀態,醫生要他休息幾天。"},{"w":"overwork","p":"v.","d":"to work too hard or too long","c":"過度工作","s":"If you overwork every day without a break, your body will eventually get sick, and your work will not improve either.","t":"如果你每天都過度工作而不休息,身體最後會生病,你的工作表現也不會變好。"},{"w":"deadline","p":"n.","d":"the latest time by which something must be finished","c":"截止期限","s":"The deadline for the science report is next Monday, but Kevin has not even started his research yet.","t":"科學報告的截止期限是下週一,但凱文連研究都還沒開始。"},{"w":"workload","p":"n.","d":"the amount of work a person has to do","c":"工作量","s":"Our teacher reduced the homework workload during exam week, because she knew we were already very stressed.","t":"考試週期間老師減少了作業的工作量,因為她知道我們已經壓力很大了。"},{"w":"stressor","p":"n.","d":"something that causes stress","c":"壓力源","s":"Moving to a new school is a common stressor for teenagers, but making one good friend can make the change much easier.","t":"轉學到新學校是青少年常見的壓力源,但交到一個好朋友就能讓這個改變輕鬆許多。"},{"w":"fight-or-flight","p":"adj.","d":"describing the body's quick reaction to danger","c":"戰或逃(反應)的","s":"When a dog suddenly barked at me, my fight-or-flight response kicked in, and I jumped back before I could even think.","t":"一隻狗突然對我吠叫時,我的戰或逃反應啟動了,我還來不及思考就往後跳開。"},{"w":"immune system","p":"n.phr.","d":"the parts of the body that fight illness","c":"免疫系統","s":"Long periods of stress can weaken your immune system, so you may catch colds more easily during busy exam seasons.","t":"長期的壓力會削弱你的免疫系統,所以在忙碌的考試季節你可能更容易感冒。"},{"w":"restless","p":"adj.","d":"unable to stay still or relax","c":"焦躁不安的","s":"The children grew restless after sitting in the car for four hours, so their parents stopped at a park to let them run.","t":"孩子們在車上坐了四個小時後變得焦躁不安,所以父母在一座公園停車讓他們跑一跑。"},{"w":"jittery","p":"adj.","d":"nervous and shaky","c":"緊張不安的","s":"I drank too much coffee before the test, and I felt jittery for the whole morning, so now I only drink water.","t":"考試前我喝了太多咖啡,整個早上都覺得緊張不安,所以現在我只喝水。"},{"w":"sleepless","p":"adj.","d":"without sleep","c":"失眠的;無眠的","s":"Emma spent a sleepless night worrying about her presentation, but in the end the audience loved her ideas.","t":"艾瑪為了她的簡報擔心了一整個無眠的夜晚,但最後聽眾很喜歡她的想法。"},{"w":"migraine","p":"n.","d":"a very bad headache that can make you feel sick","c":"偏頭痛","s":"My mother gets a migraine when she is under a lot of pressure at work, and she has to lie down in a dark room.","t":"我媽媽工作壓力很大時會偏頭痛,她必須躺在黑暗的房間裡休息。"},{"w":"blood pressure","p":"n.phr.","d":"the force of blood moving through your body","c":"血壓","s":"The doctor said my grandfather's blood pressure was too high, so he should reduce stress and eat less salt.","t":"醫生說我爺爺的血壓太高,所以他應該減少壓力並少吃鹽。"},{"w":"stomachache","p":"n.","d":"a pain in your stomach","c":"胃痛;肚子痛","s":"Some students get a stomachache on the morning of a big test, although they are not really sick.","t":"有些學生在大考當天早上會肚子痛,雖然他們並沒有真的生病。"},{"w":"appetite","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that you want to eat","c":"食慾","s":"Jason lost his appetite during the stressful week of finals, and his mother worried because he barely ate dinner.","t":"傑森在期末考那個壓力很大的一週失去了食慾,他媽媽很擔心,因為他幾乎不吃晚餐。"},{"w":"breathe","p":"v.","d":"to take air into your body and let it out","c":"呼吸","s":"The coach told the players to breathe slowly before the penalty kick, and it helped them stay calm and focused.","t":"教練告訴球員們在罰球前要慢慢呼吸,這幫助他們保持冷靜和專注。"},{"w":"frazzled","p":"adj.","d":"very tired and upset because of too much to do","c":"疲憊不堪的","s":"By Friday afternoon, the new teacher felt completely frazzled, but a quiet weekend helped her recover.","t":"到了星期五下午,這位新老師覺得完全疲憊不堪,但一個安靜的週末幫助她恢復了精神。"},{"w":"hectic","p":"adj.","d":"very busy and full of activity","c":"忙亂的","s":"December is always a hectic month for shop workers, so many of them feel tired and stressed before the holidays.","t":"十二月對店員來說總是忙亂的月份,所以許多人在假期前感到疲累和有壓力。"},{"w":"demanding","p":"adj.","d":"needing a lot of time, effort or skill","c":"要求高的;費力的","s":"Nursing is a very demanding job, but many nurses say that helping patients makes all the hard work worthwhile.","t":"護理是一份非常費力的工作,但許多護理師說幫助病人讓所有的辛苦都很值得。"},{"w":"overthinking","p":"n.","d":"thinking about something too much, in a way that is not helpful","c":"想太多;過度思考","s":"Too much overthinking kept Mia awake at night, so her counsellor suggested writing her worries on paper before bed.","t":"過度思考讓米亞晚上睡不著,所以她的輔導老師建議她睡前把煩惱寫在紙上。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"Emotions & Mental Health 情緒與心理健康","cards":[{"w":"emotion","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling such as love, fear or anger","c":"情緒;情感","s":"It is normal to feel a mix of emotion before graduation, because you are excited about the future but sad to leave your friends.","t":"畢業前感受到複雜的情緒是正常的,因為你對未來感到興奮,卻又捨不得離開朋友。"},{"w":"frustration","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being upset because you cannot do something","c":"挫折感","s":"Leo shouted in frustration when his computer crashed again, and he lost the essay he had been writing all evening.","t":"里歐的電腦又當機時,他挫折地大叫,而且他弄丟了整個晚上都在寫的文章。"},{"w":"anger","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling when something is wrong or unfair","c":"憤怒","s":"Instead of showing her anger in front of the class, the teacher waited until she was calm and then spoke to the student.","t":"老師沒有在全班面前表現她的憤怒,而是等到自己冷靜下來才和那位學生談話。"},{"w":"fear","p":"n.","d":"the feeling you have when you think something bad will happen","c":"恐懼","s":"Many people have a fear of speaking in public, but regular practice can make it much less frightening.","t":"許多人對公開演講有恐懼,但經常練習可以讓它變得不那麼可怕。"},{"w":"worry","p":"v.","d":"to keep thinking about problems or bad things","c":"擔心","s":"Parents often worry about their children's grades, but too much pressure from home can make students even more stressed.","t":"父母常常擔心孩子的成績,但來自家裡的太多壓力會讓學生壓力更大。"},{"w":"guilt","p":"n.","d":"a bad feeling because you did something wrong","c":"罪惡感","s":"Sam felt a strong sense of guilt after he forgot his best friend's birthday, so he bought her a gift the next day.","t":"山姆忘了最好朋友的生日之後感到強烈的罪惡感,所以他隔天買了一份禮物給她。"},{"w":"shame","p":"n.","d":"a painful feeling that you have done something wrong or silly","c":"羞愧","s":"He felt deep shame after cheating on the quiz, and he finally told his teacher the truth.","t":"他在小考作弊後感到深深的羞愧,最後他向老師說出了實話。"},{"w":"embarrassment","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being shy or uncomfortable in front of others","c":"尷尬","s":"Her face turned red with embarrassment when she called her teacher \"Mum\" by mistake, but everyone laughed kindly.","t":"她不小心把老師叫成「媽媽」時,臉因為尷尬而漲紅,但大家都善意地笑了。"},{"w":"jealousy","p":"n.","d":"an unhappy feeling when someone has what you want","c":"嫉妒","s":"A little jealousy is natural when your friend wins a prize, but it should not stop you from congratulating her.","t":"朋友得獎時有一點嫉妒是很自然的,但這不應該阻止你恭喜她。"},{"w":"envy","p":"v.","d":"to want something that another person has","c":"羨慕","s":"I sometimes envy students who never seem nervous before exams, but I know they probably work hard too.","t":"我有時會羨慕那些考試前似乎從不緊張的同學,但我知道他們可能也很努力。"},{"w":"grief","p":"n.","d":"great sadness, especially when someone dies","c":"悲痛","s":"After his grandmother died, Ken was full of grief, so his friends visited him often and listened to his stories about her.","t":"奶奶過世後,肯滿懷悲痛,所以他的朋友們常去探望他,並聽他講關於奶奶的故事。"},{"w":"relief","p":"n.","d":"a happy feeling when something worrying ends","c":"鬆了一口氣;寬慰","s":"It was a great relief to hear that the flight was safe, because we had been waiting at the airport for hours.","t":"聽到班機平安讓我們鬆了一口氣,因為我們已經在機場等了好幾個小時。"},{"w":"contentment","p":"n.","d":"a quiet feeling of being happy and satisfied","c":"滿足","s":"My grandfather finds contentment in simple things, such as gardening and drinking tea with his old friends.","t":"我爺爺在簡單的事情中找到滿足,像是種花種菜和跟老朋友喝茶。"},{"w":"satisfaction","p":"n.","d":"a pleased feeling after you do or get what you wanted","c":"滿意;滿足感","s":"Finishing a difficult puzzle gives me a sense of satisfaction, and it also helps me forget about my worries.","t":"完成一個困難的拼圖帶給我一種滿足感,也能幫助我忘掉煩惱。"},{"w":"optimism","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that good things will happen","c":"樂觀","s":"Her optimism helped the whole team, because she always believed they could win even when they were behind.","t":"她的樂觀幫助了整個團隊,因為即使落後,她也總是相信他們能贏。"},{"w":"pessimism","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that bad things will happen","c":"悲觀","s":"There was a lot of pessimism among the players after three losses, but the coach reminded them of their past successes.","t":"輸了三場之後,球員之間瀰漫著悲觀的氣氛,但教練提醒他們過去的成功。"},{"w":"optimistic","p":"adj.","d":"hopeful that things will turn out well","c":"樂觀的","s":"Although the test was hard, Jenny felt optimistic about her score, because she had studied every chapter carefully.","t":"雖然考試很難,珍妮對她的分數感到樂觀,因為她仔細讀過了每一章。"},{"w":"pessimistic","p":"adj.","d":"expecting things to go badly","c":"悲觀的","s":"My brother is always pessimistic about job interviews, so I tell him to focus on his strengths instead.","t":"我哥哥對工作面試總是很悲觀,所以我叫他改為專注於自己的優點。"},{"w":"gloomy","p":"adj.","d":"sad and without hope","c":"憂鬱的;陰沉的","s":"The rainy weather made everyone feel gloomy, so our teacher played some cheerful music during the break.","t":"下雨的天氣讓大家都覺得陰沉憂鬱,所以老師在下課時播放了一些輕快的音樂。"},{"w":"cheerful","p":"adj.","d":"happy and friendly","c":"開朗的;愉快的","s":"The nurse was always cheerful with her patients, and her smile made the hospital feel less frightening.","t":"那位護理師對病人總是很開朗,她的微笑讓醫院顯得不那麼可怕。"},{"w":"calm","p":"adj.","d":"relaxed and not worried or excited","c":"冷靜的;平靜的","s":"Try to stay calm during the exam, because panicking will only make you forget what you have learned.","t":"考試時要盡量保持冷靜,因為驚慌只會讓你忘記學過的東西。"},{"w":"upset","p":"adj.","d":"unhappy or worried because something bad happened","c":"難過的;心煩的","s":"Lily was upset when her best friend moved to another city, but they still video-chat every weekend.","t":"莉莉最好的朋友搬到另一個城市時,她很難過,但她們每個週末仍然視訊聊天。"},{"w":"annoyed","p":"adj.","d":"a little angry","c":"惱怒的;不耐煩的","s":"I was annoyed when my little brother kept talking during my online class, so I asked him to play in another room.","t":"我上線上課時弟弟一直講話,讓我很惱怒,所以我請他去別的房間玩。"},{"w":"phobia","p":"n.","d":"a very strong fear of something","c":"恐懼症","s":"Mark has a phobia of heights, so he never goes on the glass bridge, even when his friends try to persuade him.","t":"馬克有懼高恐懼症,所以即使朋友試著說服他,他也從不走玻璃橋。"},{"w":"counsellor","p":"n.","d":"a person trained to listen and give advice about problems","c":"輔導員;諮商師","s":"If you feel stressed about school, you can talk to the school counsellor, and everything you say will be kept private.","t":"如果你對學業感到有壓力,可以找學校的輔導老師談談,你說的一切都會被保密。"},{"w":"therapist","p":"n.","d":"a person who helps people with mental or physical problems","c":"治療師","s":"After the car accident, Anna saw a therapist every week, and slowly she felt brave enough to drive again.","t":"車禍之後,安娜每週去看治療師,慢慢地她覺得有勇氣再開車了。"},{"w":"therapy","p":"n.","d":"treatment that helps someone feel better","c":"治療","s":"Talking therapy helped my cousin understand his feelings, and now he handles stress much better than before.","t":"談話治療幫助我表哥了解自己的感受,現在他處理壓力的能力比以前好多了。"},{"w":"psychologist","p":"n.","d":"a person who studies the mind and behaviour","c":"心理學家;心理師","s":"The psychologist explained that short breaks help the brain rest, so students should not study for hours without stopping.","t":"那位心理學家解釋說,短暫的休息能讓大腦休息,所以學生不應該連續讀好幾個小時都不停下來。"},{"w":"psychiatrist","p":"n.","d":"a doctor who treats mental illness","c":"精神科醫師","s":"Her family doctor sent her to a psychiatrist, because her sleeping problems had lasted for many months.","t":"她的家庭醫師把她轉介給精神科醫師,因為她的睡眠問題已經持續好幾個月了。"},{"w":"self-confidence","p":"n.","d":"belief in your own abilities","c":"自信心","s":"Joining the drama club gave Tina more self-confidence, and now she is not afraid to share her ideas in class.","t":"加入戲劇社讓蒂娜更有自信心,現在她不再害怕在課堂上分享想法。"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"Coping & Self-Care 調適與自我照顧","cards":[{"w":"relaxation","p":"n.","d":"the act of resting and becoming calm","c":"放鬆","s":"Listening to soft music is my favourite form of relaxation, and it helps me fall asleep after a long day at school.","t":"聽輕音樂是我最喜歡的放鬆方式,它幫助我在學校忙碌一整天後入睡。"},{"w":"meditation","p":"n.","d":"sitting quietly and focusing your mind to feel calm","c":"冥想","s":"Our class tried ten minutes of meditation before the test, and many students said they felt less nervous afterwards.","t":"我們班在考試前嘗試了十分鐘的冥想,許多同學說之後覺得比較不緊張了。"},{"w":"yoga","p":"n.","d":"exercises for the body and breathing that help you relax","c":"瑜伽","s":"My aunt started doing yoga twice a week, and she says her back pain and stress have both improved.","t":"我阿姨開始每週做兩次瑜伽,她說她的背痛和壓力都改善了。"},{"w":"journaling","p":"n.","d":"writing about your thoughts and feelings regularly","c":"寫日記;寫心情筆記","s":"Daily journaling helps Amy understand her feelings, because writing them down makes her problems seem smaller.","t":"每天寫心情日記幫助艾咪了解自己的感受,因為把感受寫下來讓她的問題顯得比較小。"},{"w":"hobby","p":"n.","d":"an activity you enjoy in your free time","c":"嗜好","s":"Painting is a relaxing hobby for my father, and he often paints on Sunday mornings to forget about work.","t":"畫畫是我爸爸很放鬆的嗜好,他常在星期天早上畫畫來忘掉工作。"},{"w":"workout","p":"n.","d":"a session of physical exercise","c":"運動;健身","s":"A short workout after school gives me more energy, so I can concentrate better when I do my homework.","t":"放學後短暫的運動給我更多精力,所以我寫作業時能更專心。"},{"w":"nap","p":"n.","d":"a short sleep during the day","c":"小睡;午睡","s":"A twenty-minute nap after lunch can refresh your brain, but sleeping too long may make you feel more tired.","t":"午餐後二十分鐘的小睡可以讓大腦恢復精神,但睡太久可能會讓你更累。"},{"w":"deep breathing","p":"n.phr.","d":"taking slow, full breaths to calm down","c":"深呼吸","s":"The nurse taught the children deep breathing before their injections, and most of them stayed calm and did not cry.","t":"護理師在打針前教孩子們深呼吸,大部分的孩子都保持冷靜沒有哭。"},{"w":"self-care","p":"n.","d":"things you do to protect your own health and happiness","c":"自我照顧","s":"Getting enough sleep is an important part of self-care, but many busy students ignore it during exam week.","t":"睡眠充足是自我照顧的重要部分,但許多忙碌的學生在考試週會忽略它。"},{"w":"gratitude","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being thankful","c":"感恩;感激","s":"Writing down three things you feel gratitude for each night can make you happier, and it only takes two minutes.","t":"每天晚上寫下三件讓你心懷感恩的事可以讓你更快樂,而且只需要兩分鐘。"},{"w":"positivity","p":"n.","d":"a hopeful and cheerful attitude","c":"正面態度;正能量","s":"Our coach is full of positivity, so even after a loss, the team leaves practice feeling hopeful.","t":"我們的教練充滿正能量,所以即使輸了比賽,球隊練習結束時仍然充滿希望。"},{"w":"unwind","p":"v.","d":"to relax after work or stress","c":"放鬆","s":"After a busy week, my parents like to unwind by watching a movie at home, and they turn off their phones.","t":"忙碌一週之後,我爸媽喜歡在家看電影來放鬆,而且他們會把手機關掉。"},{"w":"recharge","p":"v.","d":"to get your energy back by resting","c":"恢復精力;充電","s":"Weekend trips to the countryside help me recharge, so I feel fresh and ready when Monday comes.","t":"週末到鄉下旅行幫助我恢復精力,所以星期一來臨時我感到神清氣爽、準備就緒。"},{"w":"vent","p":"v.","d":"to express strong feelings, especially anger","c":"發洩","s":"It is healthy to vent your feelings to a trusted friend, but shouting at strangers online is not a good idea.","t":"向信任的朋友發洩情緒是健康的,但在網路上對陌生人大吼並不是好主意。"},{"w":"confide","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone a secret or private feeling","c":"吐露;傾訴","s":"Many teenagers confide in their friends rather than their parents, because they worry that adults will not understand.","t":"許多青少年會向朋友而不是父母傾訴,因為他們擔心大人不會理解。"},{"w":"reassure","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel less worried","c":"使安心","s":"The doctor reassure my mother that the operation was simple, and she finally stopped worrying.","t":"醫生向我媽媽保證手術很簡單,讓她安心,她終於不再擔心了。"},{"w":"comfort","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel better when they are sad","c":"安慰","s":"When Sarah failed her driving test, her friends comfort her with ice cream and funny stories.","t":"莎拉駕照考試沒過時,她的朋友們用冰淇淋和好笑的故事安慰她。"},{"w":"soothe","p":"v.","d":"to make someone calm or less upset","c":"撫慰;使平靜","s":"The sound of the rain soothe me, and I soon forgot about the argument I had with my brother.","t":"雨聲撫慰了我,我很快就忘了和哥哥的爭吵。"},{"w":"downtime","p":"n.","d":"time when you rest and do not work","c":"休息時間;空閒時間","s":"Students need some downtime every day, because studying all the time can lead to stress and poor sleep.","t":"學生每天都需要一些休息時間,因為一直讀書會導致壓力和睡不好。"},{"w":"getaway","p":"n.","d":"a short holiday away from home","c":"短暫度假","s":"After the busy exam period, our family took a weekend getaway to the beach, and we all came back relaxed.","t":"忙碌的考試期過後,我們家去海邊短暫度假了一個週末,大家回來時都很放鬆。"},{"w":"laughter","p":"n.","d":"the sound or act of laughing","c":"笑聲;歡笑","s":"They say laughter is the best medicine, and watching a funny show with friends really does lower my stress.","t":"人家說歡笑是最好的良藥,而和朋友一起看搞笑節目真的能降低我的壓力。"},{"w":"socialise","p":"v.","d":"to spend time with other people for fun","c":"社交;與人交往","s":"Busy students should still socialise with friends sometimes, because spending time with people they like reduces stress.","t":"忙碌的學生偶爾還是應該和朋友交際往來,因為和喜歡的人相處能減輕壓力。"},{"w":"outlet","p":"n.","d":"a way to express feelings or use energy","c":"發洩管道;出口","s":"Playing the drums is a great outlet for my anger, and my neighbours are kind enough not to complain.","t":"打鼓是我宣洩怒氣很好的出口,而且我的鄰居們很好心沒有抱怨。"},{"w":"massage","p":"n.","d":"rubbing the body to relieve pain or stress","c":"按摩","s":"My shoulders were stiff after hours at the computer, so my sister gave me a short massage, and I felt much better.","t":"在電腦前好幾個小時之後我的肩膀很僵硬,所以姊姊幫我做了簡短的按摩,我感覺好多了。"},{"w":"helpline","p":"n.","d":"a phone service that gives advice or support","c":"求助專線","s":"If you feel very upset late at night, you can call a helpline, and a trained person will listen to you.","t":"如果你深夜感到非常難過,可以打求助專線,會有受過訓練的人聽你說話。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"Motivation & Goals 動機與目標","cards":[{"w":"goal","p":"n.","d":"something you want to achieve","c":"目標","s":"My goal this year is to read twenty English books, so I read for half an hour every night before bed.","t":"我今年的目標是讀二十本英文書,所以我每晚睡前閱讀半小時。"},{"w":"ambition","p":"n.","d":"a strong wish to be successful","c":"抱負;雄心","s":"Her ambition is to become a doctor, but she knows she must study very hard to reach that dream.","t":"她的抱負是成為醫生,但她知道必須非常努力讀書才能實現那個夢想。"},{"w":"drive","p":"n.","d":"strong energy and wish to achieve something","c":"幹勁;動力","s":"Jack has the drive to succeed, so he practises the piano every day even when his friends go out to play.","t":"傑克有成功的幹勁,所以即使朋友們出去玩,他還是每天練琴。"},{"w":"determination","p":"n.","d":"not giving up even when something is difficult","c":"決心","s":"With great determination, the runner finished the marathon, although she had hurt her ankle halfway through the race.","t":"這位跑者憑著極大的決心跑完了馬拉松,雖然她在比賽途中扭傷了腳踝。"},{"w":"perseverance","p":"n.","d":"continuing to try even when progress is slow","c":"毅力;堅持不懈","s":"Learning a language takes perseverance, because you will make many mistakes before you speak it well.","t":"學習語言需要毅力,因為在說得流利之前你會犯很多錯。"},{"w":"willpower","p":"n.","d":"the ability to control what you do and resist temptation","c":"意志力","s":"It takes willpower to put your phone away while studying, but your grades will thank you later.","t":"讀書時把手機收起來需要意志力,但你的成績之後會感謝你。"},{"w":"self-discipline","p":"n.","d":"the ability to make yourself do things you should do","c":"自律","s":"Online learning requires a lot of self-discipline, because nobody checks whether you are really watching the lessons.","t":"線上學習需要很強的自律,因為沒有人會檢查你是否真的在看課程。"},{"w":"passion","p":"n.","d":"a very strong interest or love for something","c":"熱情;熱愛","s":"Daniel has a passion for cooking, and he dreams of opening his own small restaurant one day.","t":"丹尼爾對烹飪充滿熱情,他夢想有一天開一家屬於自己的小餐廳。"},{"w":"enthusiasm","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of being very excited and interested","c":"熱忱;熱衷","s":"The students showed great enthusiasm for the science fair, so they stayed after school to build their projects.","t":"學生們對科展展現極大的熱忱,所以他們放學後留下來製作作品。"},{"w":"effort","p":"n.","d":"the hard work you use to do something","c":"努力","s":"Our teacher praises effort more than results, because she believes hard work matters more than talent.","t":"我們老師稱讚努力多過稱讚結果,因為她相信努力比天分更重要。"},{"w":"achievement","p":"n.","d":"something good you have done through hard work","c":"成就","s":"Passing the advanced English test was a big achievement for Kelly, and her parents took her out to celebrate.","t":"通過高級英語檢定對凱莉來說是很大的成就,她爸媽帶她出去慶祝。"},{"w":"purpose","p":"n.","d":"a reason that gives your life or work meaning","c":"目的;意義","s":"Volunteering at the animal shelter gave Tom a sense of purpose, and he stopped feeling bored on weekends.","t":"在動物收容所當志工讓湯姆有了意義感,他週末不再覺得無聊。"},{"w":"curiosity","p":"n.","d":"a strong wish to know or learn something","c":"好奇心","s":"Young children are full of curiosity, and they ask \"why\" so many times that parents sometimes run out of answers.","t":"小孩子充滿好奇心,他們問好多次「為什麼」,讓父母有時都答不出來了。"},{"w":"inspiration","p":"n.","d":"something that gives you new ideas or makes you want to do something","c":"靈感;鼓舞","s":"The athlete's story was a great inspiration to the students, and many of them joined the school running team.","t":"那位運動員的故事對學生們是很大的鼓舞,許多人加入了學校的跑步隊。"},{"w":"praise","p":"n.","d":"words that show you think someone did well","c":"讚美;稱讚","s":"A little praise from a teacher can make a big difference, because students work harder when they feel noticed.","t":"老師的一點稱讚就能帶來很大的不同,因為學生覺得被注意到時會更努力。"},{"w":"encouragement","p":"n.","d":"words or actions that give someone confidence","c":"鼓勵","s":"With her parents' encouragement, Grace entered the singing contest, and she was surprised to reach the final round.","t":"在父母的鼓勵下,葛蕾絲參加了歌唱比賽,而她很驚訝自己進入了決賽。"},{"w":"grit","p":"n.","d":"courage and the will to keep going","c":"毅力;堅韌","s":"Research suggests that grit matters as much as talent, because people who keep trying often achieve more.","t":"研究顯示堅韌的毅力和天分一樣重要,因為持續嘗試的人往往成就更多。"},{"w":"setback","p":"n.","d":"a problem that delays your progress","c":"挫折;阻礙","s":"Failing the first driving test was a setback, but Eric practised more and passed easily the second time.","t":"第一次駕照考試沒過是個挫折,但艾瑞克多加練習,第二次就輕鬆通過了。"},{"w":"failure","p":"n.","d":"a lack of success","c":"失敗","s":"Don't see failure as the end, because every mistake teaches you something useful for next time.","t":"不要把失敗看作終點,因為每個錯誤都會教你一些下次有用的東西。"},{"w":"progress","p":"n.","d":"movement towards a goal or improvement","c":"進步;進展","s":"Keep a list of new words you learn each week, and you will see how much progress you have made by the end of the term.","t":"把每週學到的新單字列成清單,到學期末你就會看到自己有多大的進步。"},{"w":"mindset","p":"n.","d":"a person's usual way of thinking","c":"心態;思維方式","s":"Students with a positive mindset see hard problems as chances to learn, while others may give up too quickly.","t":"擁有正向心態的學生把難題看作學習的機會,而其他人可能太快放棄。"},{"w":"self-belief","p":"n.","d":"confidence in your own abilities","c":"自信;相信自己","s":"Winning the speech contest gave Ivy more self-belief, and she began to answer questions in class without fear.","t":"贏得演講比賽讓艾薇更相信自己,她開始毫不畏懼地在課堂上回答問題。"},{"w":"competitive","p":"adj.","d":"wanting very much to win or be better than others","c":"好勝的;競爭的","s":"My brother is very competitive, so he gets upset when he loses even a simple card game with the family.","t":"我弟弟非常好勝,所以連跟家人玩簡單的紙牌遊戲輸了他都會不高興。"},{"w":"eager","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to do something very much","c":"渴望的;熱切的","s":"The new students were eager to make friends, so they joined several clubs during the first week of school.","t":"新生們渴望交朋友,所以他們在開學第一週就加入了好幾個社團。"},{"w":"keen","p":"adj.","d":"very interested and enthusiastic","c":"熱衷的;渴望的","s":"Tom is keen on basketball, and he practises shooting every evening, even when it is cold outside.","t":"湯姆熱衷於籃球,他每天傍晚都練習投籃,即使外面很冷也一樣。"},{"w":"hardworking","p":"adj.","d":"putting a lot of effort into work","c":"勤奮的","s":"My classmate is so hardworking that she reviews her notes on the bus, so she rarely needs to study late at night.","t":"我的同學非常勤奮,她在公車上複習筆記,所以她很少需要熬夜讀書。"},{"w":"lazy","p":"adj.","d":"not wanting to work or make an effort","c":"懶惰的","s":"I felt lazy on Sunday morning and stayed in bed, but then I had to rush to finish my homework at night.","t":"星期天早上我覺得很懶,一直賴在床上,結果晚上必須趕著完成作業。"},{"w":"boredom","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being tired because nothing is interesting","c":"無聊;厭倦","s":"Some students check their phones out of boredom, but this habit can make it hard to concentrate in class.","t":"有些學生出於無聊而查看手機,但這個習慣會讓上課難以專心。"},{"w":"self-motivated","p":"adj.","d":"able to work hard without others pushing you","c":"自動自發的","s":"Ken is very self-motivated, so he studies English online every day even though nobody tells him to.","t":"肯非常自動自發,所以即使沒有人要求,他每天都在線上學英文。"},{"w":"focus","p":"v.","d":"to give all your attention to one thing","c":"專注","s":"It is hard to focus on your homework when the TV is on, so find a quiet place and turn off your phone.","t":"電視開著的時候很難專注在作業上,所以找個安靜的地方並把手機關掉。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"Procrastination & Habits 拖延與習慣","cards":[{"w":"procrastinate","p":"v.","d":"to delay doing something you should do","c":"拖延","s":"I often procrastinate when I have a big essay to write, so I now break it into small parts and do one each day.","t":"我有一篇大論文要寫時常常會拖延,所以現在我把它分成小部分,每天完成一部分。"},{"w":"procrastination","p":"n.","d":"the habit of delaying things you should do","c":"拖延(症)","s":"procrastination is a common problem among students, and it often leads to stress the night before a deadline.","t":"拖延是學生常見的問題,它常常導致截止日前一晚壓力很大。"},{"w":"postpone","p":"v.","d":"to move an event to a later time","c":"延期;延後","s":"The school decided to postpone the sports day because of the typhoon, and students were happy to have an extra week to practise.","t":"學校因為颱風決定延後運動會,學生們很高興多了一週可以練習。"},{"w":"delay","p":"v.","d":"to make something happen later than planned","c":"延遲;耽擱","s":"If you delay starting your project, you will have less time to fix mistakes, and the result may disappoint you.","t":"如果你延遲開始你的專題,你修正錯誤的時間就會變少,結果可能讓你失望。"},{"w":"habit","p":"n.","d":"something you do regularly, often without thinking","c":"習慣","s":"Checking her phone first thing in the morning became a bad habit, so Lucy now keeps it outside her bedroom.","t":"一早醒來就查看手機成了一個壞習慣,所以露西現在把手機放在臥室外面。"},{"w":"habitual","p":"adj.","d":"done often or regularly as a habit","c":"習慣性的","s":"He is a habitual late-comer, and his teacher finally called his parents because he missed the first class every Monday.","t":"他是個習慣性遲到的人,老師最後打電話給他的父母,因為他每週一都錯過第一節課。"},{"w":"temptation","p":"n.","d":"a strong wish to do something you should not do","c":"誘惑","s":"The temptation to play games was strong, but Kevin finished his maths homework first and then relaxed.","t":"打電動的誘惑很強,但凱文先完成數學作業,然後才放鬆。"},{"w":"tempt","p":"v.","d":"to make someone want to do something, often something wrong","c":"引誘;吸引","s":"The smell of fried chicken tempt me to stop at the night market, although I had promised to eat healthily this week.","t":"炸雞的香味引誘我在夜市停下來,雖然我答應過這週要吃得健康。"},{"w":"schedule","p":"n.","d":"a plan that lists times for activities","c":"時間表;行程","s":"Making a weekly study schedule helped me balance homework and basketball, and I felt much less stressed.","t":"擬定每週讀書時間表幫助我平衡作業和籃球,我覺得壓力小了很多。"},{"w":"timetable","p":"n.","d":"a list of times when classes or events happen","c":"課表;時刻表","s":"Our class timetable changed this term, so now we have English first thing on Monday, which everyone finds hard.","t":"我們班這學期的課表改了,所以現在星期一第一節就是英文,大家都覺得很辛苦。"},{"w":"planner","p":"n.","d":"a small book for writing plans and dates","c":"計畫本;記事本","s":"I write all my tests and deadlines in a planner, and checking it every morning keeps me from forgetting anything.","t":"我把所有的考試和截止日期寫在計畫本裡,每天早上查看它讓我不會忘記任何事。"},{"w":"to-do list","p":"n.phr.","d":"a list of tasks you need to do","c":"待辦清單","s":"I make a to-do list every Sunday night, and crossing off each finished task gives me a nice feeling.","t":"我每個星期天晚上都會列一張待辦清單,每劃掉一項完成的事就讓我感覺很好。"},{"w":"reminder","p":"n.","d":"something that helps you remember","c":"提醒(物)","s":"I set a phone reminder for my dentist appointment, because I had forgotten it twice before.","t":"我在手機上設定了看牙醫的提醒,因為我之前已經忘記過兩次了。"},{"w":"checklist","p":"n.","d":"a list of things to check or do","c":"檢查清單","s":"Before every trip, my mother uses a checklist to pack, so we never forget passports or phone chargers.","t":"每次出遊前,我媽媽都用檢查清單打包,所以我們從不會忘記護照或手機充電器。"},{"w":"avoidance","p":"n.","d":"staying away from something you do not want to face","c":"逃避;迴避","s":"Playing games all night was just avoidance, because Tim did not want to think about his poor test result.","t":"整晚打電動只是一種逃避,因為提姆不想去想他很差的考試成績。"},{"w":"excuse","p":"n.","d":"a reason you give to explain a mistake or avoid something","c":"藉口","s":"Andy always has an excuse for not doing his homework, but this time his teacher did not believe him.","t":"安迪總是有不寫作業的藉口,但這次老師不相信他了。"},{"w":"last-minute","p":"adj.","d":"done at the latest possible time","c":"最後一刻的;臨時的","s":"last-minute studying rarely works well, because your brain needs time and sleep to remember new information.","t":"臨時抱佛腳的讀書很少有好效果,因為大腦需要時間和睡眠來記住新資訊。"},{"w":"cram","p":"v.","d":"to study a lot in a short time before an exam","c":"臨時抱佛腳;死記硬背","s":"Many students cram the night before a test, but they often forget most of the information a week later.","t":"許多學生在考試前一晚死記硬背,但一週後他們往往忘了大部分的內容。"},{"w":"self-control","p":"n.","d":"the ability to control your feelings and actions","c":"自制力","s":"It takes self-control to stop watching videos after one episode, so I ask my sister to hide the remote control.","t":"看完一集影片就停下來需要自制力,所以我請姊姊把遙控器藏起來。"},{"w":"streak","p":"n.","d":"a series of successes or days in a row","c":"連續紀錄","s":"I have a sixty-day streak on my language app, and I don't want to lose it, so I practise even on holidays.","t":"我在語言學習應用程式上有六十天的連續紀錄,我不想中斷,所以連假日也練習。"},{"w":"craving","p":"n.","d":"a very strong wish for something, often food","c":"渴望;癮","s":"Stress can give people a craving for sweet snacks, so I keep fruit on my desk during exam week.","t":"壓力會讓人渴望甜食,所以考試週時我在書桌上放水果。"},{"w":"idle","p":"adj.","d":"not working or doing anything useful","c":"閒置的;無所事事的","s":"Rather than sitting idle during the long summer holiday, Mia took a part-time job at a bookshop.","t":"米亞沒有在漫長的暑假裡無所事事,而是在一家書店找了份兼職工作。"},{"w":"dawdle","p":"v.","d":"to move or act very slowly","c":"磨蹭;拖拖拉拉","s":"If you dawdle on the way to school, you will miss the bus, and then you will be late for the test.","t":"如果你上學途中拖拖拉拉,你會錯過公車,然後考試就會遲到。"},{"w":"perfectionism","p":"n.","d":"the need to make everything perfect","c":"完美主義","s":"Her perfectionism made her rewrite the first page ten times, so she never finished the rest of the story.","t":"她的完美主義讓她把第一頁重寫了十次,所以她一直沒寫完故事的其他部分。"},{"w":"perfectionist","p":"n.","d":"a person who wants everything to be perfect","c":"完美主義者","s":"As a perfectionist, Leo spends hours on small details, but he sometimes misses deadlines because of this.","t":"身為完美主義者,里歐花好幾個小時在小細節上,但他有時因此錯過截止期限。"}]},{"unit":6,"theme":"Decision-Making & Judgement 決策與判斷","cards":[{"w":"decision","p":"n.","d":"a choice you make after thinking","c":"決定","s":"Choosing a university is a big decision, so you should talk to teachers and visit the campus before you decide.","t":"選擇大學是個重大的決定,所以你在決定之前應該和老師談談並參觀校園。"},{"w":"choice","p":"n.","d":"the act of picking one thing from several","c":"選擇","s":"There were too many choice on the menu, and it took my friend twenty minutes to order a simple drink.","t":"菜單上有太多選擇,我的朋友花了二十分鐘才點了一杯簡單的飲料。"},{"w":"judgement","p":"n.","d":"the ability to make good decisions","c":"判斷(力)","s":"Lack of sleep can affect your judgement, so you should never drive when you feel very tired.","t":"睡眠不足會影響你的判斷力,所以覺得很累時千萬不要開車。"},{"w":"heuristic","p":"n.","d":"a simple rule that helps you decide quickly","c":"捷思法;經驗法則","s":"People often use a simple heuristic when shopping, such as choosing the brand they know, but it does not always give the best result.","t":"人們購物時常用一種簡單的經驗法則,例如選擇熟悉的品牌,但這不一定能得到最好的結果。"},{"w":"intuition","p":"n.","d":"knowing something from feeling, not from thinking it through","c":"直覺","s":"My intuition told me something was wrong with the online offer, so I did not give my credit card number.","t":"我的直覺告訴我那個網路優惠有問題,所以我沒有提供信用卡號碼。"},{"w":"intuitive","p":"adj.","d":"based on feelings rather than facts; easy to understand","c":"直覺的;直觀的","s":"The new app is very intuitive, so even my grandmother learned to use it in a few minutes without any help.","t":"這個新的應用程式非常直觀,所以連我奶奶都在幾分鐘內不靠任何幫忙就學會使用了。"},{"w":"irrational","p":"adj.","d":"not based on clear thinking","c":"不理性的","s":"Her fear of the dark is irrational, but it still makes her feel nervous when she walks home at night.","t":"她對黑暗的恐懼是不理性的,但這仍然讓她晚上走路回家時感到緊張。"},{"w":"reasoning","p":"n.","d":"the process of thinking about something in a logical way","c":"推理;論證","s":"The teacher liked Jason's reasoning in his essay, because each point was supported by clear examples.","t":"老師喜歡傑森文章中的論證,因為每個論點都有清楚的例子支持。"},{"w":"logical","p":"adj.","d":"following clear and sensible thinking","c":"合乎邏輯的","s":"It is logical to compare prices before buying a new phone, but many people buy on impulse instead.","t":"買新手機前比較價格是合乎邏輯的,但許多人反而一時衝動就買了。"},{"w":"hasty","p":"adj.","d":"done too quickly without enough thought","c":"草率的;倉促的","s":"Don't make a hasty decision about quitting the team, because you might feel differently after a good night's sleep.","t":"不要草率決定退出球隊,因為好好睡一晚之後你可能會有不同的感覺。"},{"w":"gamble","p":"n.","d":"a risky action that may succeed or fail","c":"冒險;賭注","s":"Leaving his stable job to start a café was a gamble, but Mr Lin was willing to take the risk.","t":"辭掉穩定的工作去開咖啡店是一場賭注,但林先生願意冒這個險。"},{"w":"trade-off","p":"n.","d":"a balance between two things you cannot have together","c":"權衡;取捨","s":"There is always a trade-off between time and money, because a faster train usually costs more than a slow bus.","t":"時間和金錢之間總是有取捨,因為較快的火車通常比慢速巴士貴。"},{"w":"regret","p":"v.","d":"to feel sorry about something you did or did not do","c":"後悔","s":"I regret not studying harder in junior high, but I am working much harder now that I am in senior high.","t":"我後悔國中時沒有更努力讀書,但現在上了高中我努力多了。"},{"w":"hindsight","p":"n.","d":"understanding a situation only after it has happened","c":"事後的領悟;後見之明","s":"With hindsight, I should have started revising earlier, but at the time I thought I had plenty of time.","t":"事後看來,我應該早點開始複習,但當時我以為時間很充裕。"},{"w":"reckless","p":"adj.","d":"doing dangerous things without thinking about the results","c":"魯莽的","s":"Riding a scooter fast in the rain is reckless, and many accidents happen because drivers ignore the danger.","t":"在雨中騎機車騎很快是很魯莽的,許多事故都是因為駕駛人忽視危險而發生。"},{"w":"overconfidence","p":"n.","d":"too much belief in your own ability","c":"過度自信","s":"His overconfidence cost him the match, because he did not prepare and thought he would win easily.","t":"他的過度自信讓他輸掉了比賽,因為他沒有準備,還以為可以輕鬆獲勝。"},{"w":"confirmation bias","p":"n.phr.","d":"the habit of only noticing facts that agree with what you already believe","c":"確認偏誤","s":"Because of confirmation bias, people often read news that supports their own opinions, and they ignore other views.","t":"由於確認偏誤,人們常常閱讀支持自己意見的新聞,而忽略其他觀點。"},{"w":"anchoring","p":"n.","d":"relying too much on the first number or fact you hear","c":"錨定效應","s":"Shops use anchoring when they show a high \"original price\" first, so the sale price looks like a great deal.","t":"商店先標出高的「原價」來運用錨定效應,讓特價看起來非常划算。"},{"w":"framing","p":"n.","d":"the way information is presented, which can change choices","c":"框架效應;表述方式","s":"The framing of the message mattered, because more people bought the yogurt labelled \"90% fat-free\" than \"10% fat\".","t":"訊息的表述方式很重要,因為標示「90%無脂」的優格比標示「10%脂肪」的賣得更多。"},{"w":"loss aversion","p":"n.phr.","d":"the tendency to fear losing more than you enjoy winning","c":"損失規避","s":"loss aversion explains why many people keep a bad investment, because selling it would mean accepting a loss.","t":"損失規避解釋了為什麼許多人會留著不好的投資,因為賣掉就代表要接受虧損。"},{"w":"sunk cost","p":"n.phr.","d":"money or time already spent that cannot be recovered","c":"沉沒成本","s":"I kept watching the boring movie because of the sunk cost of the ticket, but I just wasted two more hours.","t":"因為電影票的沉沒成本,我繼續看那部無聊的電影,但我只是又浪費了兩個小時。"},{"w":"preference","p":"n.","d":"liking one thing more than another","c":"偏好","s":"Many students have a preference for studying at night, while others focus better early in the morning.","t":"許多學生偏好在晚上讀書,而其他人則在一大早比較專心。"},{"w":"opportunity cost","p":"n.phr.","d":"what you give up when you choose something else","c":"機會成本","s":"The opportunity cost of playing games all weekend is the study time you lose, so think carefully before you start.","t":"整個週末打電動的機會成本就是你失去的讀書時間,所以開始前要仔細想想。"},{"w":"peer pressure","p":"n.phr.","d":"influence from friends to act like them","c":"同儕壓力","s":"Because of peer pressure, some teenagers try things they don't really want to do, so it is important to learn to say no.","t":"由於同儕壓力,有些青少年會嘗試他們其實不想做的事,所以學會說不是很重要的。"},{"w":"conformity","p":"n.","d":"behaving the same way as most people in a group","c":"從眾;順從","s":"Wearing a uniform shows conformity to school rules, but some students wish they could express their own style.","t":"穿制服表示遵從校規,但有些學生希望能表現自己的風格。"},{"w":"groupthink","p":"n.","d":"when a group agrees too quickly and ignores other ideas","c":"團體迷思","s":"The team fell into groupthink, because nobody wanted to argue with the leader, so they missed an obvious problem.","t":"團隊陷入了團體迷思,因為沒有人想和隊長爭論,所以他們漏掉了一個明顯的問題。"},{"w":"advice","p":"n.","d":"an opinion about what someone should do","c":"建議;忠告","s":"My older cousin gave me useful advice about choosing a major, and I felt much clearer about my future.","t":"我的表哥給了我關於選擇科系很有用的建議,我對未來感到清楚多了。"},{"w":"indecisive","p":"adj.","d":"unable to make decisions quickly","c":"優柔寡斷的","s":"My sister is so indecisive that she spent an hour choosing a T-shirt, and in the end she bought nothing.","t":"我姊姊非常優柔寡斷,她花了一個小時挑一件T恤,最後什麼都沒買。"},{"w":"dither","p":"v.","d":"to be unable to decide what to do","c":"猶豫不決","s":"If you dither too long about joining the trip, the tickets may sell out, so please decide by Friday.","t":"如果你對參加旅行猶豫不決太久,票可能會賣完,所以請在星期五前決定。"},{"w":"hesitate","p":"v.","d":"to pause before doing something because you are unsure","c":"猶豫","s":"Please don't hesitate to ask questions in class, because other students probably have the same questions too.","t":"上課時請不要猶豫提問,因為其他同學可能也有同樣的問題。"},{"w":"weigh","p":"v.","d":"to think carefully about something before deciding","c":"權衡;考慮","s":"You should weigh the costs and benefits of a part-time job, because it may take time away from your studies.","t":"你應該權衡打工的成本與好處,因為它可能會佔用你的讀書時間。"},{"w":"foresight","p":"n.","d":"the ability to plan for what will happen in the future","c":"先見之明;遠見","s":"Thanks to her mother's foresight, they had packed umbrellas, so they stayed dry when the storm suddenly arrived.","t":"多虧媽媽的先見之明,她們帶了雨傘,所以暴風雨突然來時她們沒有淋濕。"},{"w":"rash","p":"adj.","d":"done too quickly without thinking","c":"輕率的","s":"Selling his bike on the spot was a rash decision, and he regretted it the next morning when he had to walk to school.","t":"當場賣掉腳踏車是個輕率的決定,隔天早上他必須走路上學時就後悔了。"},{"w":"reconsider","p":"v.","d":"to think again about a decision","c":"重新考慮","s":"The manager asked Nina to reconsider her plan to quit, because the company did not want to lose such a good worker.","t":"經理請妮娜重新考慮她辭職的計畫,因為公司不想失去這麼好的員工。"},{"w":"second-guess","p":"v.","d":"to doubt a decision after you have made it","c":"事後懷疑;反覆猜疑","s":"Don't second-guess every answer on the test, because your first choice is often correct if you studied well.","t":"不要對考卷上的每個答案反覆懷疑,因為如果你有好好讀書,第一個選擇往往是對的。"}]},{"unit":7,"theme":"Personality & Social Behaviour 人格與社會行為","cards":[{"w":"personality","p":"n.","d":"the type of person you are, shown by how you behave","c":"個性;人格","s":"Jenny has a warm personality, so new students always feel welcome when they sit next to her.","t":"珍妮有溫暖的個性,所以新同學坐在她旁邊總是覺得很受歡迎。"},{"w":"trait","p":"n.","d":"a quality that is part of someone's character","c":"特質;特徵","s":"Patience is an important trait for teachers, because students in the same class often learn at very different speeds.","t":"耐心是老師重要的特質,因為同一班的學生學習速度常常差很多。"},{"w":"introvert","p":"n.","d":"a quiet person who gets energy from being alone","c":"內向的人","s":"As an introvert, Ryan enjoys reading alone after school, but he still likes spending time with a few close friends.","t":"身為內向的人,萊恩喜歡放學後獨自閱讀,但他還是喜歡和幾個好朋友相處。"},{"w":"extrovert","p":"n.","d":"a lively person who gets energy from being with others","c":"外向的人","s":"My best friend is a true extrovert, and she feels tired if she has to stay home alone all weekend.","t":"我最好的朋友是個真正的外向的人,如果整個週末都得獨自待在家,她會覺得很累。"},{"w":"outgoing","p":"adj.","d":"friendly and liking to meet people","c":"外向的;友善的","s":"Linda is outgoing and talks to everyone at parties, while her twin brother prefers to listen quietly.","t":"琳達很外向,在派對上和每個人聊天,而她的雙胞胎哥哥則比較喜歡安靜地聽。"},{"w":"shy","p":"adj.","d":"nervous about talking to people you don't know","c":"害羞的","s":"Tom was too shy to ask the teacher for help, so he stayed confused about the maths problem for days.","t":"湯姆太害羞了,不敢向老師求助,所以好幾天都對那道數學題感到困惑。"},{"w":"sociable","p":"adj.","d":"enjoying spending time with other people","c":"好交際的","s":"Dogs are very sociable animals, and they often feel lonely if their owners leave them alone all day.","t":"狗是非常喜歡與人相處的動物,如果主人整天把牠們單獨留下,牠們常會感到寂寞。"},{"w":"empathy","p":"n.","d":"the ability to understand how others feel","c":"同理心","s":"Good doctors show empathy to their patients, because sick people need kindness as well as medicine.","t":"好醫生會對病人展現同理心,因為生病的人除了藥物也需要關懷。"},{"w":"sympathy","p":"n.","d":"feeling sorry for someone who is in trouble","c":"同情","s":"We sent a card to show our sympathy when our teacher's father passed away, and she thanked the whole class.","t":"老師的父親過世時,我們寄了一張卡片表達同情與慰問,她向全班道謝。"},{"w":"compassion","p":"n.","d":"a strong wish to help people who are suffering","c":"憐憫;同情心","s":"The volunteers treated the homeless with compassion, and they listened to their stories as well as giving them food.","t":"志工們以慈悲心對待無家可歸的人,除了提供食物也聆聽他們的故事。"},{"w":"altruism","p":"n.","d":"caring about others more than yourself","c":"利他主義;無私","s":"Donating blood is a simple act of altruism, because you help a stranger and expect nothing in return.","t":"捐血是一種簡單的無私行為,因為你幫助陌生人而不期待任何回報。"},{"w":"selfish","p":"adj.","d":"caring only about yourself","c":"自私的","s":"It was selfish of him to eat all the snacks, and his roommates were angry because they had paid for them too.","t":"他把所有零食都吃光很自私,他的室友們很生氣,因為他們也有出錢。"},{"w":"generous","p":"adj.","d":"happy to give time, money or help to others","c":"慷慨的","s":"Our neighbour is very generous, and she often shares the vegetables from her garden with the whole street.","t":"我們的鄰居非常慷慨,她常把自家菜園的蔬菜分享給整條街的人。"},{"w":"stubborn","p":"adj.","d":"not willing to change your mind","c":"固執的","s":"My grandfather is stubborn about using his old phone, although we have bought him a new one twice.","t":"我爺爺很固執地要用他的舊手機,雖然我們已經買了兩次新手機給他。"},{"w":"impatient","p":"adj.","d":"unable to wait calmly","c":"不耐煩的;沒耐心的","s":"People become impatient when the internet is slow, and some of them close the website after only a few seconds.","t":"網路很慢時人們會變得不耐煩,有些人只等幾秒鐘就關掉網站。"},{"w":"ego","p":"n.","d":"your sense of your own importance","c":"自我;自尊心","s":"Losing the final hurt his ego, but he learned to accept defeat and train harder for next year.","t":"輸掉決賽傷了他的自尊心,但他學會接受失敗並為明年更努力訓練。"},{"w":"self-worth","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that you are a valuable person","c":"自我價值","s":"Your self-worth should not depend on your test scores, because you have many other strengths as a person.","t":"你的自我價值不應該取決於考試分數,因為身為一個人你還有許多其他優點。"},{"w":"insecure","p":"adj.","d":"not confident about yourself","c":"沒有安全感的;不自信的","s":"Social media can make teenagers feel insecure about their looks, so it is wise to limit screen time.","t":"社群媒體會讓青少年對自己的外表感到不自信,所以限制使用螢幕的時間是明智的。"},{"w":"bystander","p":"n.","d":"a person who sees something happen but is not involved","c":"旁觀者","s":"One bystander called an ambulance after the accident, while others just stood and took photos with their phones.","t":"事故發生後有一位旁觀者叫了救護車,而其他人只是站著用手機拍照。"},{"w":"obedience","p":"n.","d":"doing what you are told to do","c":"服從","s":"The dog trainer taught basic obedience to the puppies, and soon they could sit and wait on command.","t":"訓犬師教小狗們基本的服從訓練,很快牠們就能聽口令坐下和等待。"},{"w":"persuade","p":"v.","d":"to make someone agree to do something by giving reasons","c":"說服","s":"I tried to persuade my parents to let me join the school trip, and I promised to finish my homework first.","t":"我試著說服爸媽讓我參加校外旅行,並答應會先完成作業。"},{"w":"assertive","p":"adj.","d":"expressing your opinions clearly and confidently","c":"有主見的;果斷自信的","s":"Being assertive in group work is useful, but you should also listen carefully to your classmates' ideas.","t":"在小組作業中有主見很有用,但你也應該仔細聆聽同學的想法。"},{"w":"aggressive","p":"adj.","d":"behaving in an angry or violent way","c":"有攻擊性的;具侵略性的","s":"Some players become aggressive when they are losing, so the referee has to stop the game and calm them down.","t":"有些球員輸球時會變得具攻擊性,所以裁判必須暫停比賽讓他們冷靜下來。"},{"w":"reserved","p":"adj.","d":"not showing your feelings or opinions easily","c":"拘謹的;含蓄的","s":"My new classmate seemed reserved at first, but after a few weeks she became one of the funniest people in our class.","t":"我的新同學一開始看起來很拘謹,但幾週後她成了我們班最有趣的人之一。"},{"w":"easy-going","p":"adj.","d":"relaxed and not easily worried or annoyed","c":"隨和的","s":"Our homeroom teacher is very easy-going, so students feel comfortable telling her about their problems.","t":"我們的導師非常隨和,所以學生們很自在地跟她說自己的問題。"}]},{"unit":8,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 1 (analogy – disregard)","cards":[{"w":"analogy","p":"n.","d":"a comparison that explains one thing by showing how it is like another","c":"類比","s":"The teacher used an analogy to explain stress, saying the mind is like a cup that overflows if you keep pouring water into it.","t":"老師用一個類比來解釋壓力,說心靈就像一個杯子,一直倒水就會滿出來。"},{"w":"negate","p":"v.","d":"to cancel the effect of something","c":"抵消;使無效","s":"Staying up all night can negate the benefits of studying, because a tired brain cannot remember new information well.","t":"整夜不睡會抵消讀書的效果,因為疲累的大腦無法好好記住新資訊。"},{"w":"notwithstanding","p":"adv.","d":"despite this","c":"儘管如此","s":"The exam was very difficult; Sarah passed it easily notwithstanding, because she had practised with past papers for months.","t":"那次考試非常難;儘管如此,莎拉還是輕鬆通過了,因為她用考古題練習了好幾個月。"},{"w":"pose","p":"v.","d":"to create a problem or question","c":"造成;提出","s":"Too much screen time can pose a risk to teenagers' sleep, so many parents set phone rules at night.","t":"過多的螢幕時間會對青少年的睡眠造成風險,所以許多父母在晚上訂下手機規則。"},{"w":"ambivalent","p":"adj.","d":"having mixed feelings about something","c":"矛盾的;心情複雜的","s":"Kevin felt ambivalent about moving abroad, because he was excited about the new school but sad to leave his friends.","t":"凱文對出國感到心情矛盾,因為他對新學校很興奮,卻也捨不得離開朋友。"},{"w":"apprehensive","p":"adj.","d":"worried that something bad may happen","c":"憂慮的;擔心的","s":"Many students feel apprehensive about the first day of university, but most of them settle in within a few weeks.","t":"許多學生對大學第一天感到憂慮,但大多數人在幾週內就適應了。"},{"w":"astute","p":"adj.","d":"clever at understanding situations quickly","c":"精明的;敏銳的","s":"An astute teacher can notice when a student is stressed, even if the student smiles and says everything is fine.","t":"一位敏銳的老師能察覺學生何時有壓力,即使學生微笑著說一切都很好。"},{"w":"attentive","p":"adj.","d":"listening or watching carefully","c":"專心的;留意的","s":"The students were very attentive during the talk on sleep, because the speaker gave many useful and funny examples.","t":"學生們在關於睡眠的講座中非常專心,因為講者舉了許多實用又有趣的例子。"},{"w":"aversion","p":"n.","d":"a strong dislike of something","c":"厭惡;反感","s":"Some people have an aversion to risk, so they choose a safe job even when a riskier one pays more.","t":"有些人對風險有反感,所以即使有風險的工作薪水更高,他們仍選擇安穩的工作。"},{"w":"benign","p":"adj.","d":"not harmful","c":"無害的;良性的","s":"A little stress before a test is usually benign, and it can even help you stay alert and focused.","t":"考試前有一點壓力通常是無害的,甚至能幫助你保持警覺和專注。"},{"w":"coincidence","p":"n.","d":"when two things happen together by chance","c":"巧合","s":"It was a coincidence that we both chose the same university, but we were very happy to have a familiar friend there.","t":"我們都選了同一所大學是個巧合,但能在那裡有個熟悉的朋友讓我們很開心。"},{"w":"commonplace","p":"adj.","d":"happening often; not unusual","c":"司空見慣的;普遍的","s":"Online counselling has become commonplace in recent years, and many students find it easier than talking face to face.","t":"近年來線上諮商已變得普遍,許多學生覺得這比面對面談話容易。"},{"w":"compelling","p":"adj.","d":"very interesting or convincing","c":"令人信服的;引人入勝的","s":"The scientist gave compelling evidence that exercise reduces stress, so many listeners decided to start walking every day.","t":"那位科學家提出了運動能減輕壓力的有力證據,所以許多聽眾決定開始每天散步。"},{"w":"comprehension","p":"n.","d":"the ability to understand something","c":"理解(力)","s":"Stress can reduce your reading comprehension, so you may need to read a passage twice when you are very anxious.","t":"壓力會降低你的閱讀理解力,所以在很焦慮時你可能需要把文章讀兩遍。"},{"w":"conceivable","p":"adj.","d":"possible to imagine or believe","c":"可想像的;可能的","s":"It is conceivable that the test will be harder this year, so we should prepare more carefully than last year's students did.","t":"今年的考試可能會更難,所以我們應該比去年的學生準備得更仔細。"},{"w":"concur","p":"v.","d":"to agree","c":"同意","s":"Most experts concur that regular sleep is important for learning, but many teenagers still go to bed after midnight.","t":"大多數專家都同意規律的睡眠對學習很重要,但許多青少年仍然在午夜後才上床。"},{"w":"condone","p":"v.","d":"to accept bad behaviour as acceptable","c":"縱容;寬恕","s":"The school does not condone bullying, and any student who hurts others will have to meet the principal.","t":"學校不縱容霸凌,任何傷害他人的學生都必須去見校長。"},{"w":"conscious","p":"adj.","d":"aware of something","c":"意識到的;察覺的","s":"Ella was conscious of her shaking voice during the speech, but she kept going and finished with a big smile.","t":"艾拉在演講中意識到自己的聲音在發抖,但她繼續講下去,並帶著燦爛的笑容結束。"},{"w":"constructive","p":"adj.","d":"helpful and useful, meant to improve something","c":"建設性的","s":"The coach gave the players constructive comments after the game, so they knew exactly what to practise next week.","t":"教練在比賽後給球員們有建設性的意見,所以他們確切知道下週要練習什麼。"},{"w":"conviction","p":"n.","d":"a strong belief","c":"堅定的信念;確信","s":"She spoke with conviction about the value of hard work, and her words motivated many students in the hall.","t":"她以堅定的信念談論努力的價值,她的話激勵了禮堂裡許多學生。"},{"w":"counterproductive","p":"adj.","d":"having the opposite effect of what you want","c":"適得其反的","s":"Studying for ten hours without a break is counterproductive, because your brain gets tired and you remember less.","t":"連續讀十個小時不休息是適得其反的,因為大腦會疲勞,你記得的反而更少。"},{"w":"cultivate","p":"v.","d":"to develop a skill, quality or habit","c":"培養","s":"Parents can help children cultivate good study habits, and these habits will be useful for the rest of their lives.","t":"父母可以幫助孩子培養良好的讀書習慣,而這些習慣會讓他們受用一生。"},{"w":"dichotomy","p":"n.","d":"a division between two opposite things","c":"二分法;對立","s":"There is a false dichotomy between work and rest, because good rest actually makes your work better.","t":"工作與休息之間是一種錯誤的二分對立,因為好好休息其實能讓你的工作更好。"},{"w":"disposition","p":"n.","d":"a person's natural character","c":"性情;氣質","s":"My grandmother has a cheerful disposition, and she rarely worries even when life becomes difficult.","t":"我奶奶有開朗的性情,即使生活變得艱難她也很少憂慮。"},{"w":"disregard","p":"v.","d":"to ignore something","c":"忽視;不理會","s":"Many busy workers disregard the warning signs of stress, and they only see a doctor when they become ill.","t":"許多忙碌的上班族忽視壓力的警訊,直到生病才去看醫生。"}]},{"unit":9,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 2 (dubious – subconscious)","cards":[{"w":"dubious","p":"adj.","d":"not sure; probably not true or honest","c":"可疑的;半信半疑的","s":"I was dubious about the advert that promised to cure stress in one day, so I did not buy the expensive pills.","t":"我對那個保證一天就能消除壓力的廣告感到半信半疑,所以我沒有買那昂貴的藥丸。"},{"w":"erroneous","p":"adj.","d":"wrong; not correct","c":"錯誤的","s":"It is an erroneous belief that stress is always bad, because a small amount can help people perform better.","t":"認為壓力總是不好的是一種錯誤的觀念,因為少量的壓力能幫助人表現得更好。"},{"w":"evoke","p":"v.","d":"to bring a feeling or memory into your mind","c":"喚起;引起","s":"The smell of my grandmother's soup evoke happy memories, and it always makes me feel calm and safe.","t":"奶奶煮的湯的味道喚起美好的回憶,它總是讓我感到平靜和安心。"},{"w":"exaggerate","p":"v.","d":"to describe something as bigger or worse than it is","c":"誇大","s":"People under stress often exaggerate their problems, so talking to a friend can help them see things more clearly.","t":"處於壓力下的人常常誇大自己的問題,所以和朋友聊聊可以幫助他們看得更清楚。"},{"w":"excel","p":"v.","d":"to be very good at something","c":"擅長;表現優異","s":"Some students excel in exams, while others perform better in projects, so teachers should use different kinds of tests.","t":"有些學生在考試中表現優異,而有些人在專題中表現更好,所以老師應該使用不同類型的評量。"},{"w":"fulfil","p":"v.","d":"to do what you hoped or promised","c":"實現;履行","s":"He worked hard for three years, and he finally fulfil his dream of studying music in Vienna.","t":"他努力了三年,終於實現了到維也納學音樂的夢想。"},{"w":"indifferent","p":"adj.","d":"not interested or caring","c":"漠不關心的","s":"Some students seem indifferent to their grades, but they may simply be hiding their worries from others.","t":"有些學生對成績似乎漠不關心,但他們可能只是向別人隱藏自己的擔憂。"},{"w":"ingrained","p":"adj.","d":"so fixed that it is hard to change","c":"根深蒂固的","s":"Her habit of checking messages at night was so ingrained that it took months to break, but she now sleeps much better.","t":"她晚上查看訊息的習慣是如此根深蒂固,花了好幾個月才戒掉,但現在她睡得好多了。"},{"w":"instil","p":"v.","d":"to slowly make someone have a feeling or idea","c":"灌輸;逐漸培養","s":"Good coaches instil confidence in young players, and this belief helps them stay calm in difficult games.","t":"好教練會在年輕球員心中逐漸培養自信,而這份信念幫助他們在艱難的比賽中保持冷靜。"},{"w":"intervene","p":"v.","d":"to get involved to stop or change a situation","c":"介入;干預","s":"When two students started arguing loudly, the teacher had to intervene, and she helped them talk about the problem calmly.","t":"兩個學生開始大聲爭吵時,老師必須介入,她幫助他們冷靜地討論問題。"},{"w":"intimidate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel frightened or less confident","c":"使害怕;威嚇","s":"Large crowds intimidate some speakers, so they practise in front of small groups first and slowly build their confidence.","t":"大批群眾會讓一些講者感到畏懼,所以他們先在小團體面前練習,慢慢建立自信。"},{"w":"lapse","p":"n.","d":"a short time when you fail to do something well","c":"失誤;疏忽","s":"A brief lapse in concentration caused the driver to miss the red light, but luckily nobody was hurt.","t":"一時注意力疏失讓駕駛人沒注意到紅燈,但幸好沒有人受傷。"},{"w":"obsession","p":"n.","d":"thinking about something all the time","c":"著迷;執念","s":"His obsession with perfect grades made him unhappy, so his parents told him that effort mattered more than scores.","t":"他對完美成績的執念讓他不快樂,所以他的父母告訴他努力比分數更重要。"},{"w":"overestimate","p":"v.","d":"to think something is bigger or better than it is","c":"高估","s":"Students often overestimate how much they can study in one night, and then they feel disappointed when they cannot finish.","t":"學生常常高估自己一個晚上能讀多少,結果讀不完時就感到失望。"},{"w":"ponder","p":"v.","d":"to think carefully about something for a long time","c":"沉思;仔細考慮","s":"She ponder the job offer for a whole week, because it meant moving to a city where she knew nobody.","t":"她仔細考慮那份工作邀約整整一週,因為那代表她要搬到一個一個人都不認識的城市。"},{"w":"precipitate","p":"v.","d":"to make something bad happen suddenly or sooner","c":"促成;使突然發生","s":"Losing his job precipitate a difficult period in his life, but the support of his family helped him recover.","t":"失業促成了他人生中一段艱難的時期,但家人的支持幫助他重新振作。"},{"w":"preoccupied","p":"adj.","d":"thinking so much about something that you ignore other things","c":"心事重重的;全神貫注於","s":"Dad was preoccupied with work problems during dinner, so he did not hear my news about the school prize.","t":"爸爸晚餐時滿腦子都是工作上的問題,所以沒聽到我得到學校獎項的消息。"},{"w":"presumption","p":"n.","d":"something you believe is true without proof","c":"推定;假設","s":"The presumption that boys are better at maths is wrong, and it can discourage many talented girls.","t":"認為男生數學比較好的假設是錯的,而且會使許多有天分的女生灰心。"},{"w":"propensity","p":"n.","d":"a natural tendency to behave in a certain way","c":"傾向;習性","s":"Some people have a propensity to worry, so they need to practise calming techniques more than others do.","t":"有些人天生有愛擔心的傾向,所以他們比別人更需要練習放鬆的技巧。"},{"w":"proponent","p":"n.","d":"a person who supports an idea","c":"支持者;擁護者","s":"Dr Chen is a strong proponent of short daily exercise, and she says it can improve both mood and memory.","t":"陳醫師是每天短時間運動的堅定支持者,她說這可以改善情緒和記憶力。"},{"w":"reassess","p":"v.","d":"to think about something again and maybe change your opinion","c":"重新評估","s":"After failing the first test, Leo reassess his study methods, and he started using flashcards and practice questions.","t":"第一次考試不及格之後,里歐重新評估他的讀書方法,並開始使用單字卡和練習題。"},{"w":"retrospect","p":"n.","d":"thinking about a past event","c":"回顧;回想","s":"In retrospect, the stressful exam year taught me how to manage my time, so I am grateful for it now.","t":"回想起來,那壓力很大的考試年教會我如何管理時間,所以現在我很感謝那段日子。"},{"w":"spontaneous","p":"adj.","d":"done suddenly without planning","c":"自發的;即興的","s":"We made a spontaneous decision to go hiking on Saturday, and the fresh air helped us forget about our exams.","t":"我們臨時起意決定星期六去爬山,新鮮的空氣幫助我們忘掉考試。"},{"w":"stagnant","p":"adj.","d":"not moving, changing or developing","c":"停滯的","s":"His English felt stagnant after months of using the same textbook, so he started watching English videos every day.","t":"用同一本課本好幾個月後,他覺得自己的英文停滯不前,所以他開始每天看英文影片。"},{"w":"subconscious","p":"adj.","d":"happening in your mind without you knowing","c":"潛意識的","s":"Our subconscious worries can appear in our dreams, so stressful weeks often bring strange dreams at night.","t":"我們潛意識裡的擔憂會出現在夢中,所以壓力大的那幾週晚上常會做奇怪的夢。"}]},{"unit":10,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 3 (tendency – enlighten)","cards":[{"w":"tendency","p":"n.","d":"a habit of behaving in a certain way","c":"傾向","s":"Tom has a tendency to leave everything until the last minute, so his teacher helped him make a weekly plan.","t":"湯姆有把每件事都拖到最後一刻的傾向,所以老師幫他擬定每週計畫。"},{"w":"trivial","p":"adj.","d":"small and not important","c":"瑣碎的;微不足道的","s":"When you are tired, trivial problems can feel huge, but a good night's sleep often makes them seem small again.","t":"當你很累時,微不足道的問題也會感覺很嚴重,但好好睡一晚常常會讓它們又顯得很小。"},{"w":"undue","p":"adj.","d":"more than is reasonable or necessary","c":"過度的;不適當的","s":"Parents should not put undue pressure on their children, because too much stress can make learning harder.","t":"父母不應該給孩子過度的壓力,因為太多壓力會讓學習變得更困難。"},{"w":"utmost","p":"adj.","d":"the greatest possible","c":"最大的;極度的","s":"Mental health is of the utmost importance, and schools should give students time to rest as well as study.","t":"心理健康是極為重要的,學校應該讓學生有讀書也有休息的時間。"},{"w":"withstand","p":"v.","d":"to deal with something difficult without being harmed","c":"承受;抵擋","s":"Regular exercise helps the body withstand stress, so even a short walk each day can make a difference.","t":"規律運動幫助身體承受壓力,所以即使每天短暫散步也能帶來改變。"},{"w":"adversity","p":"n.","d":"a very difficult situation","c":"逆境","s":"She showed great courage in the face of adversity, and she continued her studies even after her family lost their home.","t":"她在逆境中展現極大的勇氣,即使家裡失去了房子她仍繼續學業。"},{"w":"alienate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel unfriendly or not part of a group","c":"使疏遠","s":"Constant criticism can alienate teenagers from their parents, so families should also talk about good news.","t":"不斷的批評會讓青少年和父母疏遠,所以家人之間也應該聊聊好消息。"},{"w":"burdensome","p":"adj.","d":"difficult to deal with; heavy","c":"繁重的;累贅的","s":"The extra homework felt burdensome during exam season, so the students asked their teacher for a little more time.","t":"考試季節額外的作業讓人覺得很繁重,所以學生們請老師多給一點時間。"},{"w":"candid","p":"adj.","d":"honest and direct","c":"坦白的;直率的","s":"The singer was candid about her stage fright in the interview, and many fans said her story helped them.","t":"那位歌手在訪談中坦白談到自己的怯場,許多歌迷說她的故事幫助了他們。"},{"w":"caution","p":"n.","d":"care to avoid danger or mistakes","c":"謹慎;小心","s":"You should use caution when taking advice from social media, because not everyone online is an expert.","t":"從社群媒體獲取建議時你應該謹慎,因為網路上並不是每個人都是專家。"},{"w":"cohesion","p":"n.","d":"the state of a group being united","c":"凝聚力","s":"Team-building games improved the class's cohesion, and students started helping each other with difficult homework.","t":"團隊建立遊戲提升了全班的凝聚力,學生們開始互相幫忙解決困難的作業。"},{"w":"commend","p":"v.","d":"to praise someone formally","c":"表揚;稱讚","s":"The principal commend the students for their hard work, and she gave each of them a certificate at the ceremony.","t":"校長表揚了學生們的努力,並在典禮上頒給每個人一張證書。"},{"w":"compulsion","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling that you must do something","c":"強迫;衝動","s":"Many people feel a compulsion to check their phones every few minutes, even when they are not expecting any messages.","t":"許多人覺得有一股衝動每隔幾分鐘就要查看手機,即使他們並沒有在等任何訊息。"},{"w":"contention","p":"n.","d":"an opinion that someone argues for","c":"論點;主張","s":"The writer's main contention is that rest improves performance, and she supports it with several interesting studies.","t":"作者的主要論點是休息能提升表現,她用幾項有趣的研究來支持它。"},{"w":"dependable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be trusted","c":"可靠的","s":"A dependable friend is someone who listens when you are stressed, and they don't share your secrets with others.","t":"可靠的朋友是在你有壓力時會傾聽的人,而且他們不會把你的祕密告訴別人。"},{"w":"deprive","p":"v.","d":"to take something important away from someone","c":"剝奪","s":"Late-night gaming deprive many teenagers of sleep, and they then find it hard to concentrate at school.","t":"深夜打電動剝奪了許多青少年的睡眠,導致他們在學校難以專心。"},{"w":"detract","p":"v.","d":"to make something seem less good","c":"減損;貶低","s":"One small mistake did not detract from her excellent performance, and the judges still gave her first prize.","t":"一個小失誤並沒有減損她出色的表現,評審仍然給了她第一名。"},{"w":"discretion","p":"n.","d":"the right to decide something; care in what you say","c":"斟酌決定權;謹慎","s":"Teachers have the discretion to give students extra time, and they often do so when a student is ill.","t":"老師有斟酌決定是否給學生額外時間的權力,當學生生病時他們常會這麼做。"},{"w":"disillusioned","p":"adj.","d":"disappointed because something is not as good as you believed","c":"幻滅的;失望的","s":"Many young workers become disillusioned with long hours, so they look for jobs with a better work-life balance.","t":"許多年輕上班族對長工時感到幻滅,所以他們尋找工作與生活更平衡的工作。"},{"w":"dismiss","p":"v.","d":"to decide something is not important","c":"不予理會;摒棄","s":"Don't dismiss your feelings as silly, because talking about them is the first step to feeling better.","t":"不要把你的感受當作很傻而不予理會,因為說出來是讓自己好過一點的第一步。"},{"w":"distraught","p":"adj.","d":"extremely upset and worried","c":"心煩意亂的;極度不安的","s":"The boy was distraught when he lost his dog in the park, but a kind stranger helped him find it an hour later.","t":"那個男孩在公園弄丟了狗時心煩意亂,但一位好心的陌生人一小時後幫他找到了。"},{"w":"eloquent","p":"adj.","d":"able to speak or write clearly and powerfully","c":"口才好的;有說服力的","s":"The student gave an eloquent speech about mental health, and many classmates cried because it was so honest.","t":"那位學生發表了一場關於心理健康、很有感染力的演講,許多同學哭了,因為它是如此真誠。"},{"w":"embrace","p":"v.","d":"to accept something new with enthusiasm","c":"欣然接受","s":"Successful students embrace challenges instead of avoiding them, because they see mistakes as a normal part of learning.","t":"成功的學生會欣然接受挑戰而不是逃避,因為他們把錯誤視為學習中正常的一部分。"},{"w":"endure","p":"v.","d":"to suffer something difficult for a long time","c":"忍受;忍耐","s":"Athletes must endure hours of hard training, but the joy of winning makes the pain worthwhile for many of them.","t":"運動員必須忍受好幾個小時的艱苦訓練,但對許多人來說,勝利的喜悅讓這些痛苦都值得。"},{"w":"enlighten","p":"v.","d":"to give someone more knowledge or understanding","c":"啟發;使明白","s":"The talk on sleep science really enlighten us, and many students decided to put their phones away at night.","t":"那場關於睡眠科學的演講真的啟發了我們,許多學生決定晚上把手機收起來。"}]},{"unit":11,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 4 (entitle – optimum)","cards":[{"w":"entitle","p":"v.","d":"to give someone the right to do or have something","c":"使有權利","s":"Every worker is entitle to rest breaks during the day, but some busy employees skip them to finish their tasks.","t":"每位員工都有權在白天享有休息時間,但有些忙碌的員工為了完成工作而跳過休息。"},{"w":"envision","p":"v.","d":"to imagine something that may happen in the future","c":"設想;展望","s":"Before the race, the runner likes to envision herself crossing the finish line, and this helps her feel calm and ready.","t":"比賽前,那位跑者喜歡想像自己衝過終點線,這幫助她感到冷靜並做好準備。"},{"w":"evasive","p":"adj.","d":"avoiding giving a clear answer","c":"迴避的;含糊其詞的","s":"When I asked my brother about his test, he was evasive, so I guessed that he had not done very well.","t":"我問弟弟考試考得如何時,他含糊其詞,所以我猜他考得不太好。"},{"w":"exceptional","p":"adj.","d":"unusually good","c":"傑出的;特別優秀的","s":"She showed exceptional calm during the emergency, and her quick thinking helped everyone leave the building safely.","t":"她在緊急狀況中展現了非凡的冷靜,她的機智幫助大家安全離開大樓。"},{"w":"exemplary","p":"adj.","d":"so good that others should copy it","c":"模範的;可作為榜樣的","s":"The student's behaviour was exemplary during the school trip, so the teacher asked him to help lead the next one.","t":"那位學生在校外教學期間的表現堪為模範,所以老師請他幫忙帶領下一次的活動。"},{"w":"exhilarating","p":"adj.","d":"very exciting and making you feel happy","c":"令人振奮的","s":"Riding the roller coaster was exhilarating, and for a few minutes I completely forgot about my homework.","t":"坐雲霄飛車令人非常興奮,有好幾分鐘我完全忘了作業的事。"},{"w":"fixate","p":"v.","d":"to think about one thing too much","c":"執著於;過分關注","s":"If you fixate on one bad grade, you may lose confidence, so try to look at your overall progress instead.","t":"如果你執著於一次不好的成績,可能會失去自信,所以試著改看你整體的進步。"},{"w":"fortify","p":"v.","d":"to make something stronger","c":"強化;加強","s":"A good breakfast can fortify your body for a long day of tests, so don't skip it even when you are in a hurry.","t":"一頓好的早餐能強化你的身體以應付一整天的考試,所以即使匆忙也不要跳過。"},{"w":"inclined","p":"adj.","d":"likely to do something or behave in a certain way","c":"傾向於……的","s":"Tired people are more inclined to make poor choices, so it is wise not to make big decisions late at night.","t":"疲倦的人比較傾向做出不好的選擇,所以深夜不做重大決定是明智的。"},{"w":"overdue","p":"adj.","d":"late; should have happened before now","c":"過期的;早該發生的","s":"My library book was two weeks overdue, and I had to pay a small fine because I forgot to return it.","t":"我的圖書館書已經逾期兩週了,因為我忘記歸還,只好付了一小筆罰款。"},{"w":"toll","p":"n.","d":"the bad effect that something has over time","c":"損害;代價","s":"Months of night shifts took a heavy toll on the nurse's health, so she finally asked for a day job.","t":"好幾個月的夜班對那位護理師的健康造成了嚴重的損害,所以她終於申請了白班工作。"},{"w":"outset","p":"n.","d":"the start of something","c":"開始;開端","s":"At the outset of the course, the teacher explained all the rules, so nobody was surprised by the strict deadlines.","t":"課程一開始,老師就解釋了所有規則,所以沒有人對嚴格的截止期限感到意外。"},{"w":"interplay","p":"n.","d":"the way two or more things affect each other","c":"相互作用","s":"There is a complex interplay between sleep and mood, because poor sleep makes us sad and sadness makes sleep harder.","t":"睡眠和情緒之間有複雜的相互影響,因為睡不好讓我們難過,而難過又讓人更難入睡。"},{"w":"intricacy","p":"n.","d":"a small detail that makes something complicated","c":"錯綜複雜;細節","s":"The intricacy of the human mind fascinates scientists, but there are still many things about it that we do not understand.","t":"人類心智的錯綜複雜讓科學家著迷,但關於它仍有許多我們不了解的事。"},{"w":"irrespective","p":"adv.","d":"without considering something","c":"不論;不管","s":"Everyone needs rest irrespective of their age, so both children and adults should sleep for enough hours every night.","t":"不論年齡,每個人都需要休息,所以孩子和大人每晚都應該睡足夠的時間。"},{"w":"justifiable","p":"adj.","d":"having a good reason","c":"合理的;情有可原的","s":"Her anger was justifiable because her partner did none of the group work, but she still spoke to him politely.","t":"她的憤怒是情有可原的,因為她的組員完全沒做小組作業,但她仍然禮貌地跟他說話。"},{"w":"lethargic","p":"adj.","d":"tired and without energy","c":"無精打采的;懶洋洋的","s":"I always feel lethargic after eating a huge lunch, so I now eat a smaller meal and take a short walk.","t":"吃完一頓豐盛的午餐後我總覺得無精打采,所以我現在吃少一點,並短暫散個步。"},{"w":"mediocre","p":"adj.","d":"not very good; only average","c":"平庸的;普通的","s":"His first essay was mediocre, but he read his teacher's comments carefully and the next one was much better.","t":"他的第一篇文章很普通,但他仔細看了老師的評語,下一篇就好多了。"},{"w":"merit","p":"n.","d":"a good quality that deserves praise","c":"優點;價值","s":"Each plan has its merit, so the team discussed both of them carefully before they made a final decision.","t":"每個計畫都有它的優點,所以團隊在做最後決定前仔細討論了兩個計畫。"},{"w":"misconception","p":"n.","d":"a wrong idea or belief","c":"誤解;錯誤觀念","s":"It is a common misconception that asking for help is a sign of weakness, but it actually shows strength and good sense.","t":"認為求助是軟弱的表現是常見的誤解,但其實這展現了堅強和明智。"},{"w":"mislead","p":"v.","d":"to make someone believe something false","c":"誤導","s":"The advert misled customers into thinking the drink could reduce stress, so the company had to change it.","t":"那則廣告誤導顧客以為那種飲料可以減輕壓力,所以公司必須修改它。"},{"w":"monotonous","p":"adj.","d":"boring because it never changes","c":"單調乏味的","s":"Copying words again and again is monotonous, so our teacher uses games to help us remember new vocabulary.","t":"一遍又一遍地抄寫單字很單調乏味,所以老師用遊戲幫助我們記住新單字。"},{"w":"multifaceted","p":"adj.","d":"having many different parts or sides","c":"多面向的","s":"Stress is a multifaceted problem, so the solution may involve sleep, exercise, diet and support from friends.","t":"壓力是一個多面向的問題,所以解決方法可能包括睡眠、運動、飲食以及朋友的支持。"},{"w":"obligatory","p":"adj.","d":"required by a rule","c":"必須的;義務的","s":"Attendance at the safety talk was obligatory, so every student had to sign their name at the door.","t":"參加安全講座是必須的,所以每位學生都得在門口簽名。"},{"w":"optimum","p":"adj.","d":"best; most suitable","c":"最佳的;最適宜的","s":"Scientists say the optimum amount of sleep for teenagers is about nine hours, but most of them get much less.","t":"科學家說青少年最佳的睡眠時數大約是九小時,但大多數人睡得少得多。"}]},{"unit":12,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 5 (outlook – volition)","cards":[{"w":"outlook","p":"n.","d":"a person's general attitude to life","c":"觀點;人生觀","s":"Volunteering changed her outlook on life, and she now feels thankful for the small things she has.","t":"當志工改變了她的人生觀,她現在對自己擁有的小事物心懷感激。"},{"w":"overrate","p":"v.","d":"to think something is better than it really is","c":"高估;評價過高","s":"Many people overrate the value of expensive gadgets, but simple habits like walking often improve mood more.","t":"許多人高估了昂貴電子產品的價值,但像散步這樣簡單的習慣往往更能改善心情。"},{"w":"paradoxical","p":"adj.","d":"seeming impossible because it combines opposite ideas","c":"矛盾的;似非而是的","s":"It seems paradoxical, but taking more breaks can help you finish your work faster, because your brain stays fresh.","t":"這看起來很矛盾,但多休息反而能幫助你更快完成工作,因為你的大腦能保持清醒。"},{"w":"peripheral","p":"adj.","d":"not as important as the main part","c":"次要的;周邊的","s":"Don't waste time on peripheral details in the reading test, because most questions focus on the main ideas.","t":"閱讀測驗中不要在次要細節上浪費時間,因為大多數題目都聚焦在主旨上。"},{"w":"predisposed","p":"adj.","d":"likely to behave or suffer in a certain way","c":"易於……的;有……傾向的","s":"Some people are predisposed to anxiety because of their family history, but healthy habits can still help a lot.","t":"有些人因為家族病史而容易焦慮,但健康的習慣仍然能有很大的幫助。"},{"w":"pronounced","p":"adj.","d":"very noticeable","c":"明顯的","s":"There was a pronounced improvement in her mood after she started jogging, and her friends noticed it within a week.","t":"她開始慢跑之後心情有了明顯的改善,她的朋友們一週內就注意到了。"},{"w":"quantifiable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be measured with numbers","c":"可量化的","s":"Happiness is not easily quantifiable, but researchers use surveys to compare how people feel in different countries.","t":"快樂不容易量化,但研究人員使用問卷調查來比較不同國家人們的感受。"},{"w":"receptive","p":"adj.","d":"willing to listen to new ideas","c":"樂於接受的","s":"Students are more receptive to advice when they feel respected, so teachers should speak to them kindly.","t":"學生覺得受到尊重時更樂於接受建議,所以老師應該親切地跟他們說話。"},{"w":"reckon","p":"v.","d":"to think or believe","c":"認為;估計","s":"I reckon that a short walk would help you relax, so why don't we go to the park after dinner?","t":"我認為短暫散個步能幫助你放鬆,所以我們晚餐後何不去公園走走?"},{"w":"reflect","p":"v.","d":"to think carefully about something you did","c":"反思;深思","s":"At the end of each week, I reflect on what went well and what I can do better, and I write my ideas in a notebook.","t":"每週結束時,我會反思哪些事做得好、哪些可以做得更好,並把想法寫在筆記本裡。"},{"w":"refrain","p":"v.","d":"to stop yourself from doing something","c":"克制;避免","s":"Please refrain from using your phone during the exam, or the teacher will take your paper away.","t":"考試期間請避免使用手機,否則老師會把你的考卷收走。"},{"w":"remedial","p":"adj.","d":"aimed at improving skills that are weak","c":"補救的","s":"The school offers remedial classes after school, and students who fell behind can catch up there.","t":"學校在放學後提供補救課程,落後的學生可以在那裡趕上進度。"},{"w":"restraint","p":"n.","d":"calm control over your feelings or actions","c":"克制;自制","s":"The referee showed great restraint when the angry fans shouted at him, and he calmly continued the game.","t":"生氣的球迷對裁判大吼時,他表現出極大的克制,並冷靜地繼續比賽。"},{"w":"rigidity","p":"n.","d":"being unwilling to change or adapt","c":"僵化;死板","s":"The rigidity of the old timetable caused stress, so the school made it more flexible for students with long journeys.","t":"舊課表的僵化造成了壓力,所以學校讓它對通勤時間長的學生更有彈性。"},{"w":"scrutinise","p":"v.","d":"to examine something very carefully","c":"仔細檢查;審視","s":"Before signing the contract, my father scrutinise every line, because he did not want any unpleasant surprises later.","t":"簽約前,我爸爸仔細檢查了每一行字,因為他不想之後有任何不愉快的意外。"},{"w":"sensible","p":"adj.","d":"reasonable and practical","c":"明智的;合理的","s":"It is sensible to plan your revision early, because you will feel calmer and more prepared on the day of the exam.","t":"提早規劃複習是明智的,因為考試當天你會覺得更冷靜、更有準備。"},{"w":"shortcoming","p":"n.","d":"a weakness or fault","c":"缺點;短處","s":"Everyone has shortcoming, but accepting them is the first step to improving yourself and feeling less stressed.","t":"每個人都有缺點,但接受它們是改善自己並減輕壓力的第一步。"},{"w":"signify","p":"v.","d":"to be a sign of something","c":"表示;意味著","s":"A sudden loss of interest in hobbies may signify that a friend is stressed, so it is kind to ask how they are.","t":"突然對嗜好失去興趣可能意味著朋友有壓力,所以關心問候他們近況是很貼心的。"},{"w":"subdue","p":"v.","d":"to bring a strong feeling under control","c":"抑制;克制","s":"She took a few deep breaths to subdue her anger, and then she explained calmly why she was upset.","t":"她做了幾次深呼吸來抑制怒氣,然後冷靜地解釋她為什麼不高興。"},{"w":"substantiate","p":"v.","d":"to prove something with evidence","c":"證實","s":"You must substantiate your claims with examples in your essay, or the examiner will give you a lower score.","t":"你必須在文章中用例子證實你的主張,否則閱卷老師會給你較低的分數。"},{"w":"tedious","p":"adj.","d":"long and boring","c":"冗長乏味的","s":"Filling in the forms was tedious, but my sister finished them quickly because she wanted to start her new job.","t":"填寫那些表格很冗長乏味,但我姊姊很快就填完了,因為她想趕快開始新工作。"},{"w":"tenacity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of not giving up easily","c":"堅韌;頑強","s":"The young scientist's tenacity paid off, because after many failed experiments she finally found the answer.","t":"那位年輕科學家的堅持不懈得到了回報,因為在許多次失敗的實驗後她終於找到了答案。"},{"w":"unequivocal","p":"adj.","d":"completely clear, with no doubt","c":"明確的;毫不含糊的","s":"The doctor's advice was unequivocal, so my uncle stopped smoking and started exercising the very next day.","t":"醫生的建議毫不含糊,所以我叔叔隔天就戒菸並開始運動了。"},{"w":"variance","p":"n.","d":"the amount by which things differ","c":"差異;變異","s":"There is a large variance in how much sleep students get, and those who sleep more usually get better grades.","t":"學生的睡眠時數有很大的差異,而睡得多的人通常成績比較好。"},{"w":"volition","p":"n.","d":"the power to choose for yourself","c":"自願;意志","s":"She joined the extra classes of her own volition, and nobody had to tell her to study harder.","t":"她是出於自己的意願參加額外課程的,沒有人需要叫她更用功。"}]},{"unit":13,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 6 (weary – inept)","cards":[{"w":"weary","p":"adj.","d":"very tired","c":"疲倦的;厭倦的","s":"The weary travellers finally reached the hotel after a long delay, and they went straight to bed without eating.","t":"那些疲憊的旅客在長時間延誤後終於抵達飯店,他們沒吃東西就直接上床睡覺了。"},{"w":"abstain","p":"v.","d":"to choose not to do something you enjoy","c":"戒除;克制不做","s":"My father decided to abstain from coffee for a month, and he found that he slept much better at night.","t":"我爸爸決定戒一個月的咖啡,他發現自己晚上睡得好多了。"},{"w":"accentuate","p":"v.","d":"to make something more noticeable","c":"強調;使突出","s":"Lack of sleep can accentuate negative feelings, so small problems seem much bigger when you are tired.","t":"睡眠不足會加劇負面情緒,所以你疲倦時小問題看起來會嚴重得多。"},{"w":"adept","p":"adj.","d":"very skilled at something","c":"熟練的;擅長的","s":"My mother is adept at calming people down, so neighbours often come to her when they have family problems.","t":"我媽媽很擅長安撫別人,所以鄰居們有家庭問題時常來找她。"},{"w":"affirm","p":"v.","d":"to state that something is true; to support","c":"肯定;確認","s":"Kind words from parents affirm a child's value, and this helps the child feel safe enough to try new things.","t":"父母親切的話語能肯定孩子的價值,這幫助孩子感到足夠安心去嘗試新事物。"},{"w":"allude","p":"v.","d":"to mention something in an indirect way","c":"暗指;間接提到","s":"In his speech, the principal allude to the stress of the coming exams, but he did not talk about them directly.","t":"校長在演講中間接提到即將到來的考試壓力,但他沒有直接談論。"},{"w":"ascertain","p":"v.","d":"to find out the truth about something","c":"查明;確定","s":"The teacher tried to ascertain why the student was always late, and she learned that he looked after his little sister.","t":"老師試著查明那位學生為什麼總是遲到,她得知他要照顧妹妹。"},{"w":"baffle","p":"v.","d":"to confuse someone completely","c":"使困惑","s":"The last maths question baffle everyone in the class, so the teacher explained it again step by step.","t":"最後一道數學題讓全班都困惑不已,所以老師一步一步重新講解。"},{"w":"bewilder","p":"v.","d":"to make someone very confused","c":"使迷惑;使不知所措","s":"The busy train station bewilder my grandmother, so I held her hand and guided her to the right platform.","t":"繁忙的火車站讓我奶奶不知所措,所以我牽著她的手帶她到正確的月台。"},{"w":"cognisant","p":"adj.","d":"aware of something","c":"意識到的;認知到的","s":"Teachers should be cognisant of the pressure students face, and they should not give too much homework before exams.","t":"老師應該意識到學生面臨的壓力,考試前不應該出太多作業。"},{"w":"conjecture","p":"n.","d":"an opinion based on incomplete information","c":"推測;猜想","s":"The reason for his sudden absence is only conjecture, so we should not spread rumours about him.","t":"他突然缺席的原因只是推測,所以我們不應該散播關於他的謠言。"},{"w":"steadfast","p":"adj.","d":"staying firm and loyal","c":"堅定的;不動搖的","s":"Her parents were steadfast in their support, and they never criticised her when she failed her first audition.","t":"她的父母堅定不移地支持她,她第一次試鏡失敗時他們從未責備她。"},{"w":"converge","p":"v.","d":"to come together at one point","c":"匯集;趨於一致","s":"Many different studies converge on one idea, which is that regular exercise improves both mood and memory.","t":"許多不同的研究都趨向同一個觀點,那就是規律運動能改善情緒和記憶力。"},{"w":"defer","p":"v.","d":"to delay something until later","c":"延後;推遲","s":"Some students defer their university studies for a year, so they can work, travel and decide what they really want.","t":"有些學生把大學學業延後一年,這樣他們可以工作、旅行並決定自己真正想要什麼。"},{"w":"devoid","p":"adj.","d":"completely without something","c":"完全沒有的","s":"The waiting room was cold and devoid of colour, so the hospital painted it bright yellow to help patients feel calmer.","t":"候診室冰冷又毫無色彩,所以醫院把它漆成亮黃色,幫助病人感到更平靜。"},{"w":"discord","p":"n.","d":"disagreement between people","c":"不和;紛爭","s":"There was some discord in the group about the project topic, but they finally agreed after a friendly vote.","t":"小組對專題題目有些不和,但他們在一次友善的投票後終於達成共識。"},{"w":"disparate","p":"adj.","d":"very different from each other","c":"迥然不同的","s":"The club brings together students from disparate backgrounds, and they quickly become friends through music.","t":"這個社團聚集了來自迥然不同背景的學生,他們透過音樂很快就成為朋友。"},{"w":"dormant","p":"adj.","d":"not active now but able to become active later","c":"潛伏的;休眠的","s":"Her love of painting had been dormant for years, but it came back when she joined an art class after retirement.","t":"她對繪畫的熱愛已經沉寂多年,但退休後參加美術課時又重新燃起。"},{"w":"expedite","p":"v.","d":"to make a process happen faster","c":"加快;促進","s":"The new online system will expedite the application process, so students will receive their results in days, not weeks.","t":"新的線上系統將加快申請流程,所以學生會在幾天內而不是幾週內收到結果。"},{"w":"forgo","p":"v.","d":"to choose not to have something you would like","c":"放棄;摒棄","s":"Many students forgo weekend outings before the big exam, but short breaks are still important for their health.","t":"許多學生在大考前放棄週末出遊,但短暫的休息對健康仍然很重要。"},{"w":"heed","p":"v.","d":"to pay attention to advice or a warning","c":"聽從;留意","s":"If you heed your body's warning signs, such as headaches and poor sleep, you can deal with stress before it gets worse.","t":"如果你留意身體的警訊,例如頭痛和睡不好,就能在壓力惡化之前處理它。"},{"w":"impetuous","p":"adj.","d":"acting quickly without thinking carefully","c":"衝動的;魯莽的","s":"He made an impetuous decision to quit his job after one bad day, and he regretted it when he could not pay his rent.","t":"他在糟糕的一天之後做了辭職的衝動決定,當他付不出房租時就後悔了。"},{"w":"inadvertent","p":"adj.","d":"done without meaning to","c":"無心的;不經意的","s":"Her inadvertent comment hurt her friend's feelings, so she apologised as soon as she realised what she had said.","t":"她無心的一句話傷了朋友的感情,所以她一意識到自己說了什麼就立刻道歉。"},{"w":"incessant","p":"adj.","d":"never stopping","c":"不停的;持續不斷的","s":"The incessant noise from the building site made it hard to study, so I went to the library for some peace.","t":"工地不停的噪音讓人很難讀書,所以我去圖書館找個清靜。"},{"w":"inept","p":"adj.","d":"having no skill","c":"笨拙的;無能的","s":"I felt inept at cooking when I first lived alone, but after many YouTube videos I can now make simple meals.","t":"我剛開始獨自生活時覺得自己做菜很笨拙,但看了許多影片之後,現在我能做簡單的餐點了。"}]},{"unit":14,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 7 (insatiable – synthesise)","cards":[{"w":"insatiable","p":"adj.","d":"always wanting more","c":"無法滿足的","s":"Some children have an insatiable curiosity about science, and they ask questions that even their teachers cannot answer.","t":"有些孩子對科學有永不滿足的好奇心,他們問的問題連老師都答不出來。"},{"w":"introspection","p":"n.","d":"careful thinking about your own thoughts and feelings","c":"內省;自我反省","s":"A little introspection can help you understand your stress, but too much thinking about yourself may make you more anxious.","t":"一點自我反省能幫助你了解自己的壓力,但過度思考自己可能讓你更焦慮。"},{"w":"irrevocable","p":"adj.","d":"impossible to change or undo","c":"不可撤銷的;無法挽回的","s":"Choosing a university major is important, but it is not irrevocable, because many students change their major later.","t":"選擇大學科系很重要,但並非無法挽回,因為許多學生後來會轉系。"},{"w":"latent","p":"adj.","d":"present but hidden or not yet developed","c":"潛在的;隱藏的","s":"The drama teacher discovered his latent talent for acting, and he soon became the star of the school play.","t":"戲劇老師發掘了他潛在的表演天分,他很快就成了學校話劇的主角。"},{"w":"mundane","p":"adj.","d":"ordinary and not interesting","c":"平凡的;單調的","s":"Even mundane tasks like washing dishes can be relaxing, because they give your mind a break from difficult problems.","t":"即使像洗碗這樣平凡的家務也能讓人放鬆,因為它們讓你的頭腦暫時擺脫困難的問題。"},{"w":"novice","p":"n.","d":"a person who is new to an activity","c":"新手;初學者","s":"As a novice at public speaking, Amy felt nervous, but her teacher gave her simple tips that helped a lot.","t":"身為公開演講的新手,艾咪感到很緊張,但老師給了她一些簡單又很有幫助的訣竅。"},{"w":"oblivious","p":"adj.","d":"not aware of something","c":"未察覺的;渾然不覺的","s":"He was oblivious to the time while playing his game, so he missed dinner and his mother was not happy.","t":"他打電動時渾然不覺時間的流逝,所以錯過了晚餐,他媽媽很不高興。"},{"w":"overt","p":"adj.","d":"done openly, not secretly","c":"公開的;明顯的","s":"There were no overt signs of stress, but her friends noticed that she had stopped eating lunch with them.","t":"她沒有明顯的壓力跡象,但她的朋友們注意到她不再和他們一起吃午餐了。"},{"w":"palpable","p":"adj.","d":"so strong that it can almost be felt","c":"明顯的;可感覺到的","s":"The tension in the exam hall was palpable, and nobody spoke while the teacher handed out the papers.","t":"考場裡的緊張氣氛清晰可感,老師發考卷時沒有人說話。"},{"w":"perpetual","p":"adj.","d":"never ending; happening again and again","c":"永久的;不斷的","s":"Living in a state of perpetual worry is bad for your health, so learning to relax is an important life skill.","t":"處於無止盡的擔憂狀態對健康有害,所以學會放鬆是一項重要的生活技能。"},{"w":"rejuvenate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel young or energetic again","c":"使恢復活力","s":"A week by the sea rejuvenate my parents, and they came home smiling and full of new plans.","t":"在海邊待一週讓我爸媽恢復了活力,他們帶著笑容回家,還充滿新計畫。"},{"w":"relinquish","p":"v.","d":"to give up control or a position","c":"放棄;讓出","s":"The captain decided to relinquish his role because of stress, and another player took over the team leadership.","t":"隊長因為壓力決定放棄他的職位,另一名球員接手了球隊的領導工作。"},{"w":"remorse","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of being sorry for doing something wrong","c":"悔恨;懊悔","s":"He felt deep remorse after shouting at his little sister, so he bought her favourite cake to say sorry.","t":"對妹妹大吼之後他深感懊悔,所以他買了她最愛的蛋糕來道歉。"},{"w":"repress","p":"v.","d":"to stop yourself from showing a feeling","c":"壓抑","s":"If you always repress your feelings, they may come out later in unhealthy ways, so it is better to talk about them.","t":"如果你總是壓抑自己的感受,它們之後可能會以不健康的方式爆發,所以最好說出來。"},{"w":"resent","p":"v.","d":"to feel angry about something unfair","c":"怨恨;憤慨","s":"Some students resent group projects because they end up doing most of the work, while others do very little.","t":"有些學生怨恨小組專題,因為最後大部分工作都是他們在做,而其他人做得很少。"},{"w":"respite","p":"n.","d":"a short rest from something difficult","c":"暫緩;喘息","s":"The long weekend gave the students a welcome respite from exams, and many of them spent it with their families.","t":"連假讓學生們從考試中得到難得的喘息,許多人和家人一起度過。"},{"w":"revert","p":"v.","d":"to go back to a previous state or habit","c":"恢復;回到(原狀)","s":"After the holidays, it is easy to revert to bad sleeping habits, so try to wake up at the same time every day.","t":"假期過後很容易回到不好的睡眠習慣,所以試著每天在同一時間起床。"},{"w":"rudimentary","p":"adj.","d":"very basic","c":"基本的;初步的","s":"I only have a rudimentary knowledge of Japanese, but I can order food and ask for directions when I travel.","t":"我只有基礎的日文知識,但旅行時我能點餐和問路。"},{"w":"scrupulous","p":"adj.","d":"very careful to be honest and correct","c":"一絲不苟的;嚴謹的","s":"The scientist was scrupulous about recording every result, so other researchers trusted her findings completely.","t":"那位科學家對記錄每個結果都一絲不苟,所以其他研究人員完全信任她的發現。"},{"w":"stifle","p":"v.","d":"to stop something from developing","c":"扼殺;抑制","s":"Too many rules can stifle creativity, so the art teacher lets students choose their own topics and materials.","t":"太多規則會扼殺創造力,所以美術老師讓學生自己選擇主題和材料。"},{"w":"succinct","p":"adj.","d":"clear and short","c":"簡潔的","s":"Please keep your answers succinct in the interview, because the panel has many candidates to see today.","t":"面試時請讓你的回答保持簡潔,因為評審團今天要面試很多候選人。"},{"w":"superfluous","p":"adj.","d":"more than is needed","c":"多餘的","s":"Remove any superfluous words from your essay, because clear and simple writing is easier for examiners to read.","t":"把文章中任何多餘的字刪掉,因為清楚簡單的寫作讓閱卷老師更容易閱讀。"},{"w":"surmount","p":"v.","d":"to deal with a difficulty successfully","c":"克服","s":"With the help of her tutor, she managed to surmount her fear of maths, and she even chose it as her favourite subject later.","t":"在家教的幫助下,她成功克服了對數學的恐懼,後來甚至把它選為最喜歡的科目。"},{"w":"sway","p":"v.","d":"to influence someone's opinion or decision","c":"左右;影響","s":"Advertisements can easily sway young shoppers, so it is wise to wait a day before buying something expensive.","t":"廣告很容易左右年輕購物者,所以在買昂貴的東西前先等一天是明智的。"},{"w":"synthesise","p":"v.","d":"to combine ideas or information into one","c":"綜合;整合","s":"Good students synthesise information from different sources, and they use it to write clear and balanced essays.","t":"好學生會整合來自不同來源的資訊,並用它寫出清楚而平衡的文章。"}]},{"unit":15,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 8 (tenuous – lucid)","cards":[{"w":"tenuous","p":"adj.","d":"very weak or uncertain","c":"薄弱的;站不住腳的","s":"The link between the two events was tenuous, so the teacher asked us to find stronger evidence for our argument.","t":"這兩件事之間的關聯很薄弱,所以老師要我們為論點找更有力的證據。"},{"w":"unfounded","p":"adj.","d":"not based on facts","c":"毫無根據的","s":"Her fears about the new school were unfounded, because the students were friendly and the teachers were very helpful.","t":"她對新學校的恐懼是毫無根據的,因為同學們很友善,老師們也很樂於幫忙。"},{"w":"unwavering","p":"adj.","d":"not changing or becoming weaker","c":"堅定不移的","s":"The team's unwavering belief in their coach helped them through a difficult season, and they finally won the cup.","t":"球隊對教練堅定不移的信任幫助他們度過艱難的球季,最後他們贏得了冠軍。"},{"w":"accustomed","p":"adj.","d":"used to something","c":"習慣於……的","s":"It took me a month to get accustomed to waking up early, but now I enjoy the quiet time before school.","t":"我花了一個月才習慣早起,但現在我很享受上學前的安靜時光。"},{"w":"discourage","p":"v.","d":"to make someone lose confidence or not want to do something","c":"使灰心;勸阻","s":"Don't let one bad score discourage you, because every learner has difficult days and you can still improve.","t":"不要讓一次糟糕的分數使你灰心,因為每個學習者都有不順的日子,而你仍然可以進步。"},{"w":"dismay","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of shock and disappointment","c":"驚愕;沮喪","s":"To her dismay, the bus left just as she arrived, so she had to wait thirty minutes in the rain.","t":"令她沮喪的是,她一到公車就開走了,所以她只好在雨中等了三十分鐘。"},{"w":"fervent","p":"adj.","d":"having very strong feelings about something","c":"熱烈的;熱切的","s":"My cousin is a fervent supporter of the local team, and he goes to every home game even when it rains.","t":"我表哥是當地球隊的狂熱支持者,即使下雨他也去看每一場主場比賽。"},{"w":"foremost","p":"adj.","d":"most important","c":"最重要的;首要的","s":"Your health should be your foremost concern, and no exam result is worth losing sleep for weeks.","t":"你的健康應該是你最重要的考量,沒有任何考試成績值得讓你連續好幾週失眠。"},{"w":"fortitude","p":"n.","d":"courage in pain or difficulty","c":"堅毅;剛毅","s":"The patient faced her long treatment with great fortitude, and she always smiled at the nurses.","t":"那位病人以極大的堅毅面對漫長的治療,她總是對護理師們微笑。"},{"w":"inquisitive","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to learn and ask questions","c":"好奇的;好問的","s":"inquisitive students often learn faster, because they ask questions until they really understand the topic.","t":"好問的學生通常學得比較快,因為他們會一直提問直到真正理解主題。"},{"w":"notorious","p":"adj.","d":"famous for something bad","c":"惡名昭彰的;出了名(不好)的","s":"This road is notorious for traffic jams, so my father leaves home very early to avoid being late for work.","t":"這條路以塞車出了名,所以我爸爸很早出門以免上班遲到。"},{"w":"plight","p":"n.","d":"a difficult or sad situation","c":"困境","s":"The news story about the plight of overworked delivery drivers made many people tip them more generously.","t":"關於過勞外送員困境的新聞報導,讓許多人更慷慨地給他們小費。"},{"w":"relish","p":"v.","d":"to enjoy something very much","c":"享受;喜愛","s":"Some people relish a challenge, and they feel more excited than nervous before an important game.","t":"有些人享受挑戰,在重要比賽前他們感到的是興奮多於緊張。"},{"w":"resolute","p":"adj.","d":"determined and not willing to change","c":"堅決的;果斷的","s":"She was resolute in her plan to run a marathon, so she trained every morning, even in the cold winter.","t":"她對跑馬拉松的計畫非常堅決,所以即使在寒冷的冬天她每天早上都訓練。"},{"w":"tactic","p":"n.","d":"a method used to achieve something","c":"策略;手法","s":"One useful tactic for exams is to answer the easy questions first, so you build confidence before the hard ones.","t":"考試的一個實用策略是先回答簡單的題目,這樣在面對難題前你就能建立信心。"},{"w":"unpredictable","p":"adj.","d":"changing in a way that is hard to guess","c":"難以預測的","s":"The weather in the mountains is unpredictable, so you should always bring a raincoat, even on a sunny morning.","t":"山上的天氣難以預測,所以即使是晴朗的早晨,你也應該隨身帶雨衣。"},{"w":"vague","p":"adj.","d":"not clear or detailed","c":"模糊的;含糊的","s":"My goals were too vague last year, so this year I wrote specific plans with dates and small steps.","t":"我去年的目標太模糊了,所以今年我寫下了有日期和小步驟的具體計畫。"},{"w":"worthwhile","p":"adj.","d":"worth the time, money or effort","c":"值得的","s":"Learning to manage stress is worthwhile, because it will help you in school, at work and in your relationships.","t":"學習管理壓力是值得的,因為它會在學業、工作和人際關係中幫助你。"},{"w":"stamina","p":"n.","d":"the energy to keep doing something for a long time","c":"耐力;精力","s":"Long exams require mental stamina, so students should practise with full-length tests before the real exam.","t":"長時間的考試需要心理上的耐力,所以學生在正式考試前應該用完整長度的測驗練習。"},{"w":"vitality","p":"n.","d":"energy and liveliness","c":"活力","s":"Regular exercise gives older people more vitality, and many of them say they feel ten years younger.","t":"規律運動讓年長者更有活力,許多人說他們覺得自己年輕了十歲。"},{"w":"mentality","p":"n.","d":"a typical way of thinking","c":"心態;思維模式","s":"A winning mentality helps athletes stay calm under pressure, but they also need good training and rest.","t":"贏家心態幫助運動員在壓力下保持冷靜,但他們也需要良好的訓練和休息。"},{"w":"reminiscent","p":"adj.","d":"making you think of something in the past","c":"使人聯想起……的","s":"The smell of the new classroom was reminiscent of my first day at primary school, and it made me feel a little nervous.","t":"新教室的氣味讓我聯想起小學第一天上學,這讓我感到有點緊張。"},{"w":"reproach","p":"v.","d":"to criticise someone, often gently","c":"責備","s":"Don't reproach yourself for every small mistake, because being kind to yourself makes it easier to improve.","t":"不要為每個小錯誤責備自己,因為善待自己會讓進步變得更容易。"},{"w":"compulsory","p":"adj.","d":"required by law or rules","c":"義務的;強制的","s":"Physical education is compulsory in most schools, and it gives students a healthy break from sitting in class.","t":"體育課在大多數學校是必修的,它讓學生從久坐的課堂中得到健康的休息。"},{"w":"lucid","p":"adj.","d":"clear and easy to understand","c":"清晰易懂的","s":"The teacher gave a lucid explanation of the grammar rule, so even the weakest students could follow it.","t":"老師對這個文法規則做了清晰易懂的解釋,所以連程度最弱的學生都能理解。"}]},{"unit":16,"theme":"Fixed Phrases & Collocations 固定片語與搭配詞","cards":[{"w":"under pressure","p":"adj.phr.","d":"feeling stressed because of demands","c":"承受壓力","s":"Many students perform badly under pressure, so teachers give them practice tests to make the real exam feel familiar.","t":"許多學生在壓力下表現不佳,所以老師讓他們做模擬考,使正式考試感覺比較熟悉。"},{"w":"stressed out","p":"adj.phr.","d":"very worried and tense","c":"壓力很大的","s":"I was so stressed out before my final exams that I could not sleep, so my mum made me a cup of warm milk.","t":"期末考前我壓力大到睡不著,所以媽媽幫我泡了一杯熱牛奶。"},{"w":"burn the midnight oil","p":"v.phr.","d":"to work or study late at night","c":"熬夜工作或讀書","s":"Jason had to burn the midnight oil to finish his project, and he looked very tired in class the next morning.","t":"傑森必須熬夜苦讀才能完成他的專題,隔天早上他在課堂上看起來非常疲倦。"},{"w":"keep one's cool","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stay calm in a difficult situation","c":"保持冷靜","s":"The pilot keep one's cool when the engine failed, and she landed the plane safely in a nearby field.","t":"引擎故障時那位機長保持冷靜,並把飛機安全降落在附近的田野上。"},{"w":"lose one's temper","p":"v.phr.","d":"to suddenly become very angry","c":"發脾氣","s":"My father rarely lose one's temper, but he shouted when my brother broke the window for the second time.","t":"我爸爸很少發脾氣,但我弟弟第二次打破窗戶時他大吼了。"},{"w":"put off","p":"v.phr.","d":"to delay doing something","c":"拖延;延後","s":"I always put off cleaning my room until the weekend, and by then it is so messy that it takes hours.","t":"我總是把打掃房間拖延到週末,到那時房間亂到要花好幾個小時才能整理好。"},{"w":"let off steam","p":"v.phr.","d":"to release strong feelings or energy","c":"發洩情緒或精力","s":"After a long day of exams, the students played basketball to let off steam, and they all felt better afterwards.","t":"經過一整天的考試,學生們打籃球來發洩情緒,之後大家都覺得好多了。"},{"w":"bite off more than one can chew","p":"v.phr.","d":"to try to do more than you are able to","c":"貪多嚼不爛;不自量力","s":"Lucy joined four clubs this term, but she bite off more than one can chew, so she quit two of them.","t":"露西這學期參加了四個社團,但她貪多嚼不爛,所以退出了其中兩個。"},{"w":"sit on the fence","p":"v.phr.","d":"to avoid choosing between two sides","c":"保持中立;騎牆觀望","s":"You can't sit on the fence forever, because the team needs your vote before we can start the project.","t":"你不能永遠騎牆觀望,因為我們開始專題之前,團隊需要你投下一票。"},{"w":"make up one's mind","p":"v.phr.","d":"to decide","c":"下定決心;做決定","s":"I couldn't make up one's mind about which dress to buy, so I asked my sister to choose for me.","t":"我無法決定要買哪件洋裝,所以我請姊姊幫我選。"},{"w":"sleep on it","p":"v.phr.","d":"to wait until the next day before deciding","c":"考慮一晚再決定","s":"The job offer sounded exciting, but my mother told me to sleep on it before I gave the company an answer.","t":"那份工作邀約聽起來很令人興奮,但媽媽叫我先考慮一晚再給公司答覆。"},{"w":"go with one's gut","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a decision based on feelings","c":"憑直覺行事","s":"When you are not sure of an answer, it is often best to go with one's gut, because your first idea is usually right.","t":"當你不確定答案時,憑直覺通常是最好的,因為你的第一個想法往往是對的。"},{"w":"have second thoughts","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start to doubt a decision","c":"改變主意;猶豫","s":"Mark agreed to sing at the concert, but he began to have second thoughts when he saw how big the audience was.","t":"馬克答應在音樂會上唱歌,但當他看到觀眾有多少時,他開始猶豫要不要改變主意。"},{"w":"jump to conclusions","p":"v.phr.","d":"to decide something is true too quickly","c":"妄下結論","s":"Don't jump to conclusions when a friend does not reply quickly, because they may simply be busy with homework.","t":"朋友沒有很快回覆時不要妄下結論,因為他們可能只是在忙作業。"},{"w":"go the extra mile","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make more effort than is expected","c":"加倍努力;多付出一些","s":"Our English teacher always go the extra mile for her students, and she even stays after school to answer questions.","t":"我們的英文老師總是為學生加倍付出,她甚至放學後留下來回答問題。"},{"w":"light at the end of the tunnel","p":"n.phr.","d":"a sign that a difficult time will end soon","c":"黑暗盡頭的曙光;苦盡甘來的希望","s":"Exams finish next Friday, so we can finally see the light at the end of the tunnel, and we are planning a party.","t":"考試下週五結束,所以我們終於看到了隧道盡頭的曙光,我們正在計畫辦派對。"},{"w":"take it easy","p":"v.phr.","d":"to relax and not work too hard","c":"放輕鬆;別太累","s":"The doctor told my mother to take it easy for a week, so we all helped with the cooking and cleaning.","t":"醫生叫我媽媽好好休息一週,所以我們大家都幫忙煮飯和打掃。"},{"w":"a weight off one's shoulders","p":"n.phr.","d":"relief from a worry or responsibility","c":"如釋重負","s":"Handing in my final report was a weight off one's shoulders, and I slept for ten hours that night.","t":"交出期末報告讓我如釋重負,那天晚上我睡了十個小時。"},{"w":"get cold feet","p":"v.phr.","d":"to suddenly feel too nervous to do something you planned","c":"臨陣退縮","s":"Tina planned to try out for the school play, but she get cold feet at the last moment and stayed home.","t":"蒂娜原本打算參加學校話劇的試鏡,但她在最後一刻臨陣退縮,待在家裡。"},{"w":"at the end of one's tether","p":"adj.phr.","d":"so tired or upset that you cannot cope any more","c":"束手無策;忍無可忍","s":"After a week of noisy neighbours and little sleep, I was at the end of one's tether, so I asked them politely to be quiet.","t":"經過一週吵鬧的鄰居和很少的睡眠,我已經忍無可忍,所以我禮貌地請他們安靜一點。"}]}];
